\s1 Job’s Character and Wealth
\r (\ref James 5:7–12|JAS 5:7-12\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb There was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb in the land|בְאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Uz|ע֖וּץ\rb* \rb whose name was|שְׁמ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Job|אִיּ֣וֹב\rb*. \rb And this man|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb was|וְהָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb blameless|תָּ֧ם\rb* \rb and upright|וְיָשָׁ֛ר\rb*, \rb fearing|וִירֵ֥א\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and shunning|וְסָ֥ר\rb* \rb evil|מֵרָֽע׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb |וַיִּוָּ֥לְדוּ\rb* \rb He had seven|שִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and three|וְשָׁל֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb daughters|בָּנֽוֹת׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb and he owned|וַיְהִ֣י\rb*\rb |מִ֠קְנֵהוּ\rb* \rb 7,000|שִֽׁבְעַ֨ת\rb*\rb |אַלְפֵי־\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֜אן\rb*, \rb 3,000|וּשְׁלֹ֧שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אַלְפֵ֣י\rb* \rb camels|גְמַלִּ֗ים\rb*, \rb 500|וַחֲמֵ֨שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֤וֹת\rb* \rb yoke|צֶֽמֶד־\rb* \rb of oxen|בָּקָר֙\rb*, \rb 500|וַחֲמֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb female donkeys|אֲתוֹנ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and a very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb*\rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb large number of|רַבָּ֣ה\rb* \rb servants|וַעֲבֻדָּ֖ה\rb*. \rb Job was the|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb greatest|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the people|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of the East|קֶֽדֶם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Job’s sons|בָנָיו֙\rb* \rb would take turns|וְהָלְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb holding|וְעָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb feasts|מִשְׁתֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb in their homes|בֵּ֖ית\rb*,\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |יוֹמ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and they would invite|וְשָׁלְח֗וּ\rb*\rb |וְקָרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb their three|לִשְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb sisters|אַחְיֹתֵיהֶם\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb and drink|וְלִשְׁתּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb with them|עִמָּהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb And|וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb when|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֨י\rb* \rb of feasting|הַמִּשְׁתֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb were over|הִקִּיפֽוּ֩\rb*, \rb Job|אִיּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb would send for his children|וַיִּשְׁלַ֧ח\rb* \rb to purify them|וַֽיְקַדְּשֵׁ֗ם\rb*, \rb rising early|וְהִשְׁכִּ֣ים\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּקֶר֮\rb* \rb to offer|וְהֶעֱלָ֣ה\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹלוֹת֮\rb*\rb |מִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb for all of them|כֻּלָּם֒\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb Job|אִיּ֔וֹב\rb* \rb thought|אָמַ֣ר\rb*, “\rb Perhaps|אוּלַי֙\rb* \rb my children|בָנַ֔י\rb* \rb have sinned|חָטְא֣וּ\rb* \rb and cursed|וּבֵרֲכ֥וּ\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb in their hearts|בִּלְבָבָ֑ם\rb*.” \rb This|כָּ֛כָה\rb* \rb was Job’s|אִיּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb regular|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb practice|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*.
\s1 Satan’s First Attack
\p \v 6 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb One day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to present themselves|לְהִתְיַצֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb before|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֖ן\rb*\f + \fr 1:6 \ft That is, \fqa the Accuser \ft or \fqa the Adversary\ft ; here and throughout Job 1\f* \rb also|גַֽם־\rb* \rb came|וַיָּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb with them|בְּתוֹכָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 “\rb Where|מֵאַ֣יִן\rb* \rb have you come from|תָּבֹ֑א\rb*?” \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֖ן\rb*.
\p “\rb From roaming|מִשּׁ֣וּט\rb* \rb through the earth|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*,” \rb he|הַשָּׂטָ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*, “\rb and walking back and forth|וּמֵֽהִתְהַלֵּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in it|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֔ן\rb*, “\rb Have you considered|הֲשַׂ֥מְתָּ\rb*\rb |לִבְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֣י\rb* \rb Job|אִיּ֑וֹב\rb*? \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there is no one|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb on earth|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb like him|כָּמֹ֙הוּ֙\rb*, \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb who is blameless|תָּ֧ם\rb* \rb and upright|וְיָשָׁ֛ר\rb*, \rb who fears|יְרֵ֥א\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and shuns|וְסָ֥ר\rb* \rb evil|מֵרָֽע׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֧עַן\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* “\rb Does Job|אִיּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb fear|יָרֵ֥א\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb for nothing|הַֽחִנָּ֔ם\rb*? \v 10 \rb Have You not|הֲלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |אַתְּ\rb* \rb placed a hedge|שַׂ֣כְתָּ\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִ֑יב\rb* \rb around him|בַעֲד֧וֹ\rb*\rb |וּבְעַד־\rb* \rb and his household|בֵּית֛וֹ\rb* \rb and|וּבְעַ֥ד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he owns|ל֖וֹ\rb*? \rb You have blessed|בֵּרַ֔כְתָּ\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb* \rb of his hands|יָדָיו֙\rb*, \rb and his possessions|וּמִקְנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb have increased|פָּרַ֥ץ\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb But|וְאוּלָם֙\rb* \rb stretch out|שְֽׁלַֽח־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb Your hand|יָֽדְךָ֔\rb* \rb and strike|וְגַ֖ע\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has|ל֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he will surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb curse You|יְבָרֲכֶֽךָּ׃\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb Your face|פָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”
\p \v 12 “\rb Very well|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֗ן\rb*. “\rb Everything|כָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has is|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb in your hands|בְּיָדֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb but|רַ֣ק\rb* \rb you must not|אַל־\rb* \rb lay|תִּשְׁלַ֖ח\rb* \rb a hand|יָדֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb on the man himself|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*.”
\p \rb Then Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֔ן\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֖ם\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb from the presence|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 Job Loses His Children and Possessions
\p \v 13 \rb |וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb One day|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*, \rb while Job’s sons|וּבָנָ֨יו\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֹתָ֤יו\rb* \rb were eating|אֹֽכְלִים֙\rb* \rb and drinking|וְשֹׁתִ֣ים\rb* \rb wine|יַ֔יִן\rb* \rb in their oldest|הַבְּכֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb brother’s|אֲחִיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb house|בְּבֵ֖ית\rb*, \v 14 \rb a messenger|וּמַלְאָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb and reported|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Job|אִיּ֖וֹב\rb*: “\rb While the oxen|הַבָּקָר֙\rb* \rb were|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb plowing|חֹֽרְשׁ֔וֹת\rb* \rb and the donkeys|וְהָאֲתֹנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb were grazing|רֹע֥וֹת\rb* \rb nearby|עַל־\rb*\rb |יְדֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb the Sabeans|שְׁבָא֙\rb* \rb swooped down|וַתִּפֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb and took them away|וַתִּקָּחֵ֔ם\rb*.\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb They put|הִכּ֣וּ\rb* \rb the servants|הַנְּעָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb and I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדִּ֖י\rb* \rb have escaped|וָֽאִמָּ֨לְטָ֧ה\rb*\rb |רַק־\rb* \rb to tell|לְהַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 16 \rb While he|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb was still|ע֣וֹד׀\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֵּ֗ר\rb*, \rb another|וְזֶה֮\rb* \rb messenger came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb and reported|וַיֹּאמַר֒\rb*: “\rb The fire|אֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb fell|נָֽפְלָה֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*. \rb It burned|וַתִּבְעַ֥ר\rb* \rb and consumed|וַתֹּאכְלֵ֑ם\rb* \rb the sheep|בַּצֹּ֛אן\rb* \rb and the servants|וּבַנְּעָרִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדִּ֖י\rb* \rb have escaped|וָאִמָּ֨לְטָ֧ה\rb*\rb |רַק־\rb* \rb to tell|לְהַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 17 \rb While he|ע֣וֹד׀\rb* \rb was still|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֵּ֗ר\rb*, \rb another messenger|וְזֶה֮\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb and reported|וַיֹּאמַר֒\rb*: “\rb The Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּ֞ים\rb* \rb formed|שָׂ֣מוּ׀\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb bands|רָאשִׁ֗ים\rb*, \rb raided|וַֽיִּפְשְׁט֤וּ\rb* \rb the camels|הַגְּמַלִּים֙\rb*, \rb and took them away|וַיִּקָּח֔וּם\rb*.\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb They put|הִכּ֣וּ\rb* \rb the servants|הַנְּעָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb and I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדִּ֖י\rb* \rb have escaped|וָאִמָּ֨לְטָ֧ה\rb*\rb |רַק־\rb* \rb to tell|לְהַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 18 \rb While|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb he|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb was still speaking|מְדַבֵּ֔ר\rb*, \rb another messenger|וְזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb and reported|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*: “\rb Your sons|בָּנֶ֨יךָ\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנוֹתֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb were eating|אֹֽכְלִים֙\rb* \rb and drinking|וְשֹׁתִ֣ים\rb* \rb wine|יַ֔יִן\rb* \rb in their oldest|הַבְּכֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb brother’s|אֲחִיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb house|בְּבֵ֖ית\rb*, \v 19 \rb when suddenly|וְהִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb a mighty|גְּדוֹלָ֜ה\rb* \rb wind|ר֨וּחַ\rb* \rb swept in|בָּ֣אָה׀\rb* \rb from|מֵעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the desert|הַמִּדְבָּ֗ר\rb* \rb and struck|וַיִּגַּע֙\rb* \rb the four|בְּאַרְבַּע֙\rb* \rb corners|פִּנּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb*. \rb It collapsed|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the young people|הַנְּעָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and they are dead|וַיָּמ֑וּתוּ\rb*, \rb and I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדִּ֖י\rb* \rb have escaped|וָאִמָּ֨לְטָ֧ה\rb*\rb |רַק־\rb* \rb to tell|לְהַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 20 \rb Then Job|אִיּוֹב֙\rb* \rb stood up|וַיָּ֤קָם\rb*, \rb tore|וַיִּקְרַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his robe|מְעִל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and shaved|וַיָּ֖גָז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb He fell|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb to the ground|אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb and worshiped|וַיִּשְׁתָּֽחוּ׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb saying|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Naked|עָרֹ֨ם\rb* \rb I came|יָצָתִי\rb* \rb from my mother’s|אִמִּ֗י\rb* \rb womb|מִבֶּ֣טֶן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and naked|וְעָרֹם֙\rb* \rb I will return|אָשׁ֣וּב\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔מָה\rb*.
\q1 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֔ן\rb*, \rb and the LORD|וַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has taken away|לָקָ֑ח\rb*.
\q2 \rb Blessed|מְבֹרָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb be|יְהִ֛י\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb In all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֖את\rb*, \rb Job|אִיּ֑וֹב\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb sin|חָטָ֣א\rb* \rb or|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb charge|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb with wrongdoing|תִּפְלָ֖ה\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 Job Loses His Health
\p \v 1 \rb On another|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to present themselves|לְהִתְיַצֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb before|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and Satan|הַשָּׂטָן֙\rb*\f + \fr 2:1 \ft That is, \fqa the Accuser \ft or \fqa the Adversary\ft ; here and throughout Job 2\f* \rb also|גַֽם־\rb* \rb came|וַיָּב֤וֹא\rb* \rb with them|בְּתֹכָ֔ם\rb* \rb to present himself|לְהִתְיַצֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb before|עַל־\rb* \rb Him|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 “\rb Where|אֵ֥י\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb have you come from|תָּבֹ֑א\rb*?” \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֔ן\rb*.
\p “\rb From roaming|מִשֻּׁ֣ט\rb* \rb through the earth|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*,” \rb he|הַשָּׂטָ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb and walking back and forth|וּמֵהִתְהַלֵּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in it|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֗ן\rb*, “\rb Have you considered|הֲשַׂ֣מְתָּ\rb*\rb |לִבְּךָ֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֣י\rb* \rb Job|אִיּוֹב֒\rb*? \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb there is no one|אֵ֨ין\rb* \rb on earth|בָּאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb like him|כָּמֹ֜הוּ\rb*, \rb a man who is|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb blameless|תָּ֧ם\rb* \rb and upright|וְיָשָׁ֛ר\rb*, \rb who fears|יְרֵ֥א\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and shuns|וְסָ֣ר\rb* \rb evil|מֵרָ֑ע\rb*. \rb He still|וְעֹדֶ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb retains|מַחֲזִ֣יק\rb* \rb his integrity|בְּתֻמָּת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb even though you incited Me|וַתְּסִיתֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb against him|ב֖וֹ\rb* \rb to ruin him|לְבַלְּע֥וֹ\rb* \rb without cause|חִנָּֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 “\rb Skin|ע֣וֹר\rb* \rb for|בְּעַד־\rb* \rb skin|ע֗וֹר\rb*!”\rb |יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֧עַן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*. “\rb A man|לָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb will give up|יִתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb he owns|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in exchange for|בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb But|אוּלָם֙\rb* \rb stretch out|שְֽׁלַֽח־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb Your hand|יָֽדְךָ֔\rb* \rb and strike|וְגַ֥ע\rb* \rb his flesh|בְּשָׂר֑וֹ\rb* \rb and bones|עַצְמ֖וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and he will surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb curse You|יְבָרֲכֶֽךָּ׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Your face|פָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”
\p \v 6 “\rb Very well|הִנּ֣וֹ\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֖ן\rb*. “\rb He is in your hands|בְיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb but|אַ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you must spare|שְׁמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁ֥וֹ\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb So Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֔ן\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb from the presence|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and infected|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Job|אִיּוֹב֙\rb* \rb with terrible|רָ֔ע\rb* \rb boils|בִּשְׁחִ֣ין\rb* \rb from the soles|מִכַּ֥ף\rb* \rb of his feet|רַגְל֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַד\rb* \rb the crown of his head|קָדְקֳדֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb And Job took|וַיִּֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb a piece of broken pottery|חֶ֔רֶשׂ\rb* \rb to scrape|לְהִתְגָּרֵ֖ד\rb* \rb himself|בּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb as he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb sat|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb among|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the ashes|הָאֵֽפֶר׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then Job’s wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb Do you still|עֹדְךָ֖\rb* \rb retain|מַחֲזִ֣יק\rb* \rb your integrity|בְּתֻמָּתֶ֑ךָ\rb*? \rb Curse|בָּרֵ֥ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 2:9 \ft Or \fqa Bless\f* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and die|וָמֻֽת׃\rb*!”
\p \v 10 “\rb You speak|כְּדַבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb as a|אַחַ֤ת\rb* \rb foolish woman|הַנְּבָלוֹת֙\rb* \rb speaks|תְּדַבֵּ֔רִי\rb*,”\rb |גַּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb her|אֵלֶ֗יהָ\rb*. “\rb Should we accept|נְקַבֵּל֙\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb only good|הַטּ֗וֹב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and not|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |נְקַבֵּ֑ל\rb* \rb adversity|הָרָ֖ע\rb*?”
\p \rb In all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֛את\rb*, \rb Job|אִיּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb sin|חָטָ֥א\rb* \rb in what he said|בִּשְׂפָתָֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Job’s Three Friends
\p \v 11 \rb Now when Job’s|אִיּ֗וֹב\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת׀\rb* \rb friends|רֵעֵ֣י\rb*— \rb Eliphaz|אֱלִיפַ֤ז\rb* \rb the Temanite|הַתֵּימָנִי֙\rb*, \rb Bildad|וּבִלְדַּ֣ד\rb* \rb the Shuhite|הַשּׁוּחִ֔י\rb*, \rb and Zophar|וְצוֹפַ֖ר\rb* \rb the Naamathite|הַנַּֽעֲמָתִ֑י\rb*— \rb heard|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֞וּ\rb* \rb about all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֮\rb* \rb adversity|הָרָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb that had come|הַבָּ֣אָה\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָיו֒\rb*, \rb each of them|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb from his home|מִמְּקֹמ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and they met|וַיִּוָּעֲד֣וּ\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֔ו\rb* \rb to go|לָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb and sympathize|לָנֽוּד־\rb* \rb with Job|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb and comfort him|וּֽלְנַחֲמֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb When they lifted up|וַיִּשְׂא֨וּ\rb* \rb their eyes|עֵינֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb from afar|מֵרָחוֹק֙\rb*, \rb they could barely|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb recognize Job|הִכִּירֻ֔הוּ\rb*. \rb They began to weep|וַיִּבְכּ֑וּ\rb* \rb aloud|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb*\rb |קוֹלָ֖ם\rb*, \rb and each man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb tore|וַֽיִּקְרְעוּ֙\rb* \rb his robe|מְעִל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and threw|וַיִּזְרְק֥וּ\rb* \rb dust|עָפָ֛ר\rb* \rb in the air|הַשָּׁמָֽיְמָה׃\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רָאשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 13 \rb Then they sat|וַיֵּשְׁב֤וּ\rb* \rb on the ground|לָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb with him|אִתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and seven|וְשִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb nights|לֵיל֑וֹת\rb*, \rb but no|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb one spoke|דֹּבֵ֤ר\rb* \rb a word|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they saw|רָא֔וּ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb how intense|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb his suffering|הַכְּאֵ֖ב\rb* \rb was|גָדַ֥ל\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 Job Laments His Birth
\p \v 1 \rb After|אַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb this|כֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb Job|אִיּוֹב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb opened|פָּתַ֤ח\rb* \rb his mouth|פִּ֔יהוּ\rb* \rb and cursed|וַיְקַלֵּ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the day of his birth|יוֹמֽוֹ׃פ\rb*. \v 2 \rb And this is what|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb* \rb he|אִיּ֗וֹב\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 3 “\rb May the day|י֭וֹם\rb* \rb of my birth|אִוָּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb perish|יֹ֣אבַד\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the night|וְהַלַּ֥יְלָה\rb* \rb it was said|אָ֝מַ֗ר\rb*,
\q2 ‘\rb A boy|גָֽבֶר׃\rb* \rb is conceived|הֹ֣רָה\rb*.’
\q1 \v 4 \rb If only that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb had turned|יְֽהִ֫י\rb* \rb to darkness|חֹ֥שֶׁךְ\rb*!
\q2 \rb May God|אֱל֣וֹהַּ\rb* \rb above|מִמָּ֑עַל\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb*\rb |אַֽל־\rb* \rb disregard it|יִדְרְשֵׁ֣הוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb may no light|נְהָרָֽה׃\rb* \rb shine|תּוֹפַ֖ע\rb* \rb upon it|עָלָ֣יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb May darkness|חֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb and gloom|וְ֭צַלְמָוֶת\rb* \rb reclaim it|יִגְאָלֻ֡הוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and a cloud|עֲנָנָ֑ה\rb* \rb settle|תִּשְׁכָּן־\rb* \rb over it|עָלָ֣יו\rb*;
\q2 \rb may the blackness|כִּֽמְרִ֥ירֵי\rb* \rb of the day|יֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb overwhelm it|יְ֝בַעֲתֻ֗הוּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb If only darkness|אֹ֥פֶל\rb* \rb had taken|הַהוּא֮\rb* \rb that night|הַלַּ֥יְלָה\rb* \rb away|יִקָּחֵ֪ה֫וּ\rb*!
\q2 \rb May it not|אַל־\rb* \rb appear|יִ֭חַדְּ\rb* \rb among the days|בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the year|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb may it never|אַל־\rb* \rb be entered|יָבֹֽא׃\rb* \rb in any|בְּמִסְפַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of the months|יְ֝רָחִ֗ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb Behold|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb may that|הַ֭הוּא\rb* \rb night|הַלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb be|יְהִ֣י\rb* \rb barren|גַלְמ֑וּד\rb*;
\q2 \rb may no|אַל־\rb* \rb joyful voice|רְנָנָ֣ה\rb* \rb come|תָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb into it|בֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb May it be cursed|אֹרְרֵי־\rb* \rb by those who curse|יִקְּבֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the day|י֑וֹם\rb*\f + \fr 3:8 \ft Or \fqa curse the sea\f* —
\q2 \rb those prepared|הָ֝עֲתִידִ֗ים\rb* \rb to rouse|עֹרֵ֥ר\rb* \rb Leviathan|לִוְיָתָֽן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb May its morning|נִ֫שְׁפּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb stars|כּוֹכְבֵ֪י\rb* \rb grow dark|יֶחְשְׁכוּ֮\rb*;
\q2 \rb may it wait|יְקַו־\rb* \rb in vain|וָאַ֑יִן\rb* \rb for daylight|לְא֥וֹר\rb*;
\q2 \rb may it not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb see|יִ֝רְאֶ֗ה\rb* \rb the breaking|בְּעַפְעַפֵּי־\rb* \rb of dawn|שָֽׁחַר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb that night did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb shut|סָ֭גַר\rb* \rb the doors|דַּלְתֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the womb|בִטְנִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb to hide|וַיַּסְתֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb the sorrow|עָ֝מָ֗ל\rb* \rb from my eyes|מֵעֵינָֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb*\rb |לֹּ֣א\rb* \rb did I not perish|אָמ֑וּת\rb* \rb at birth|מֵרֶ֣חֶם\rb*;
\q2 \rb why did I not die|וְאֶגְוָֽע׃\rb* \rb as I came|יָצָ֣אתִי\rb* \rb from the womb|מִבֶּ֖טֶן\rb*?
\q1 \v 12 \rb Why|מַ֭דּוּעַ\rb* \rb were there knees|בִרְכָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb to receive me|קִדְּמ֣וּנִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and|וּמַה־\rb* \rb breasts|שָּׁ֝דַ֗יִם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I should be nursed|אִינָֽק׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 13 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb now|עַ֭תָּה\rb* \rb I would be lying down|שָׁכַ֣בְתִּי\rb* \rb in peace|וְאֶשְׁק֑וֹט\rb*;
\q2 \rb I would be asleep|יָ֝שַׁ֗נְתִּי\rb* \rb and|אָ֤ז׀\rb* \rb at rest|יָנ֬וּחַֽ\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb kings|מְ֭לָכִים\rb* \rb and counselors|וְיֹ֣עֲצֵי\rb* \rb of the earth|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb who built|הַבֹּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb for themselves|לָֽמוֹ׃\rb* \rb cities now in ruins|חֳרָב֣וֹת\rb*,
\q1 \v 15 \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb princes|שָׂ֭רִים\rb* \rb who had gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb who filled|הַֽמְמַלְאִ֖ים\rb* \rb their houses|בָּתֵּיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb with silver|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb Or|א֤וֹ\rb* \rb why was|אֶהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb I not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb hidden|טָ֭מוּן\rb* \rb like a stillborn child|כְנֵ֣פֶל\rb*,
\q2 \rb like an infant|כְּ֝עֹלְלִ֗ים\rb* \rb who never|לֹא־\rb* \rb sees|רָ֥אוּ\rb* \rb daylight|אֽוֹר׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 17 \rb There|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb the wicked|רְ֭שָׁעִים\rb* \rb cease|חָ֣דְלוּ\rb* \rb from raging|רֹ֑גֶז\rb*,
\q2 \rb and there|וְשָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb the weary|יְגִ֣יעֵי\rb*\rb |כֹֽחַ׃\rb* \rb find rest|יָ֝נ֗וּחוּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb The captives|אֲסִירִ֣ים\rb* \rb enjoy|יַ֭חַד\rb* \rb their ease|שַׁאֲנָ֑נוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb they do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb hear|שָׁ֝מְע֗וּ\rb* \rb the voice|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the oppressor|נֹגֵֽשׂ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb Both small|קָטֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and great|וְ֭גָדוֹל\rb* \rb are there|שָׁ֣ם\rb*\rb |ה֑וּא\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the slave|וְ֝עֶ֗בֶד\rb* \rb is freed|חָפְשִׁ֥י\rb* \rb from his master|מֵאֲדֹנָֽיו׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb is light|א֑וֹר\rb* \rb given|יִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb to the miserable|לְעָמֵ֣ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and life|וְ֝חַיִּ֗ים\rb* \rb to the bitter|לְמָ֣רֵי\rb* \rb of soul|נָֽפֶשׁ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 21 \rb who long|הַֽמְחַכִּ֣ים\rb* \rb for death|לַמָּ֣וֶת\rb* \rb that does not come|וְאֵינֶ֑נּוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and search for it|וַֽ֝יַּחְפְּרֻ֗הוּ\rb* \rb like hidden treasure|מִמַּטְמוֹנִֽים׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 22 \rb who rejoice|הַשְּׂמֵחִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֱלֵי־\rb* \rb and greatly|גִ֑יל\rb* \rb exult|יָ֝שִׂ֗ישׂוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb when|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they reach|יִמְצְאוּ־\rb* \rb the grave|קָֽבֶר׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 23 \rb Why is life given to a man|לְ֭גֶבֶר\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb way|דַּרְכּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb is hidden|נִסְתָּ֑רָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb whom God|אֱל֣וֹהַּ\rb*\rb |בַּעֲדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb has hedged in|וַיָּ֖סֶךְ\rb*?
\q1 \v 24 \rb I sigh|אַנְחָתִ֣י\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb food|לַ֭חְמִי\rb* \rb is put|תָבֹ֑א\rb* \rb before me|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my groans|שַׁאֲגֹתָֽי׃\rb* \rb pour out|וַֽיִּתְּכ֥וּ\rb* \rb like water|כַ֝מַּ֗יִם\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the thing|פַ֣חַד\rb* \rb I feared|פָּ֭חַדְתִּי\rb* \rb has overtaken me|וַיֶּאֱתָיֵ֑נִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and what|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I dreaded|יָ֝גֹ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb has befallen|יָ֣בֹא\rb* \rb me|לִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb I am not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb at ease|שָׁלַ֨וְתִּי׀\rb* \rb or quiet|שָׁקַ֥טְתִּי\rb*\rb |וְֽלֹא־\rb*;
\q2 \rb I have no|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb rest|נָ֗חְתִּי\rb*, \rb for trouble|רֹֽגֶז׃פ\rb* \rb has come|וַיָּ֥בֹא\rb*.”
\c 4
\s1 Eliphaz: The Innocent Prosper
\p \v 1 \rb Then Eliphaz|אֱלִיפַ֥ז\rb* \rb the Temanite|הַֽתֵּימָנִ֗י\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb* \rb replied|וַ֭יַּעַן\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb If one ventures|הֲנִסָּ֬ה\rb* \rb a word|דָבָ֣ר\rb* \rb with you|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb*, \rb will you be wearied|תִּלְאֶ֑ה\rb*?
\q2 \rb Yet who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb can|יוּכָֽל׃\rb* \rb keep|וַעְצֹ֥ר\rb* \rb from speaking|בְּ֝מִלִּ֗ין\rb*?
\q1 \v 3 \rb Surely|הִ֭נֵּה\rb* \rb you have instructed|יִסַּ֣רְתָּ\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and have strengthened|תְּחַזֵּֽק׃\rb* \rb their feeble|רָפ֣וֹת\rb* \rb hands|וְיָדַ֖יִם\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb Your words|מִלֶּ֑יךָ\rb* \rb have steadied|יְקִימ֣וּן\rb* \rb those who stumbled|כּ֭וֹשֵׁל\rb*;
\q2 \rb you have braced|תְּאַמֵּֽץ׃\rb* \rb the knees|וּבִרְכַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb that were buckling|כֹּרְע֣וֹת\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb But|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֨ה׀\rb* \rb trouble has come|תָּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb upon you|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb*, \rb and you are weary|וַתֵּ֑לֶא\rb*.
\q2 \rb It strikes you|תִּגַּ֥ע\rb*,\rb |עָ֝דֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb and you are dismayed|וַתִּבָּהֵֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Is your reverence|יִ֭רְאָתְךָ\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹ֣א\rb* \rb your confidence|כִּסְלָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the uprightness|וְתֹ֣ם\rb* \rb of your ways|דְּרָכֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb your hope|תִּ֝קְוָתְךָ֗\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb Consider|זְכָר־\rb* \rb now, I plead|נָ֗א\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb Who|מִ֤י\rb*,\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb being innocent|נָקִ֣י\rb*, \rb has ever perished|אָבָ֑ד\rb*?
\q2 \rb Or where|וְ֝אֵיפֹ֗ה\rb* \rb have the upright|יְשָׁרִ֥ים\rb* \rb been destroyed|נִכְחָֽדוּ׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 8 \rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have observed|רָ֭אִיתִי\rb*, \rb those who plow|חֹ֣רְשֵׁי\rb* \rb iniquity|אָ֑וֶן\rb*
\q2 \rb and those who sow|וְזֹרְעֵ֖י\rb* \rb trouble|עָמָ֣ל\rb* \rb reap the same|יִקְצְרֻֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb By the breath|מִנִּשְׁמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of God|אֱל֣וֹהַ\rb* \rb they perish|יֹאבֵ֑דוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and by the blast|וּמֵר֖וּחַ\rb* \rb of His anger|אַפּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb they are consumed|יִכְלֽוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb The lion|אַ֭רְיֵה\rb* \rb may roar|שַׁאֲגַ֣ת\rb*, \rb and the fierce lion|שָׁ֑חַל\rb* \rb may growl|וְק֣וֹל\rb*,
\q2 \rb yet the teeth|וְשִׁנֵּ֖י\rb* \rb of the young lions|כְפִירִ֣ים\rb* \rb are broken|נִתָּֽעוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb The old lion|לַ֭יִשׁ\rb* \rb perishes|אֹבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb for lack|מִבְּלִי־\rb* \rb of prey|טָ֑רֶף\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the cubs|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the lioness|לָ֝בִ֗יא\rb* \rb are scattered|יִתְפָּרָֽדוּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb Now a word|דָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb came to me|וְ֭אֵלַי\rb* \rb secretly|יְגֻנָּ֑ב\rb*;
\q2 \rb my ears|אָ֝זְנִ֗י\rb* \rb caught|וַתִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a whisper|שֵׁ֣מֶץ\rb* \rb of it|מֶֽנְהֽוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb In disquieting|בִּ֭שְׂעִפִּים\rb* \rb visions|מֵחֶזְיֹנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb in the night|לָ֑יְלָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb when deep sleep|תַּ֝רְדֵּמָ֗ה\rb* \rb falls|בִּנְפֹ֥ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִֽׁים׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 14 \rb fear|פַּ֣חַד\rb* \rb and trembling|וּרְעָדָ֑ה\rb* \rb came over me|קְ֭רָאַנִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and made all|וְרֹ֖ב\rb* \rb my bones|עַצְמוֹתַ֣י\rb* \rb shudder|הִפְחִֽיד׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb Then a spirit|וְ֭רוּחַ\rb*\f + \fr 4:15 \ft Or \fqa a wind\f* \rb glided|יַחֲלֹ֑ף\rb* \rb past|עַל־\rb* \rb my face|פָּנַ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the hair|שַֽׂעֲרַ֥ת\rb* \rb on my body|בְּשָׂרִֽי׃\rb* \rb bristled|תְּ֝סַמֵּ֗ר\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb It stood still|יַעֲמֹ֤ד׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb but I could not|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb discern|אַכִּ֬יר\rb* \rb its appearance|מַרְאֵ֗הוּ\rb*;
\q1 \rb a form|תְּ֭מוּנָה\rb* \rb loomed before|לְנֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb my eyes|עֵינָ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I heard|אֶשְׁמָֽע׃\rb* \rb a whispering|דְּמָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb voice|וָק֣וֹל\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 17 ‘\rb Can a mortal|הַֽ֭אֱנוֹשׁ\rb* \rb be more righteous|יִצְדָּ֑ק\rb* \rb than God|מֵאֱל֣וֹהַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb or|אִ֥ם\rb* \rb a man|גָּֽבֶר׃\rb* \rb more pure|יִטְהַר־\rb* \rb than his Maker|מֵ֝עֹשֵׂ֗הוּ\rb*?
\q1 \v 18 \rb If|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb God puts no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb trust|יַאֲמִ֑ין\rb* \rb in His servants|בַּ֭עֲבָדָיו\rb*,
\q2 \rb and He charges|יָשִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb His angels|וּ֝בְמַלְאָכָ֗יו\rb* \rb with error|תָּהֳלָֽה׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 19 \rb how much more|אַ֤ף׀\rb* \rb those who dwell|שֹׁכְנֵ֬י\rb* \rb in houses|בָֽתֵּי־\rb* \rb of clay|חֹ֗מֶר\rb*,
\q2 \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb foundations|יְסוֹדָ֑ם\rb* \rb are in the dust|בֶּעָפָ֥ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb who can be crushed|יְ֝דַכְּא֗וּם\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵי־\rb* \rb like a moth|עָֽשׁ׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 20 \rb They are smashed to pieces|יֻכַּ֑תּוּ\rb* \rb from dawn|מִבֹּ֣קֶר\rb* \rb to dusk|לָעֶ֣רֶב\rb*;
\q2 \rb unnoticed|מִבְּלִ֥י\rb*\rb |מֵ֝שִׂ֗ים\rb*, \rb they perish|יֹאבֵֽדוּ׃\rb* \rb forever|לָנֶ֥צַח\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb Are not their tent cords|יִתְרָ֣ם\rb*\rb |הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb pulled up|נִסַּ֣ע\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that they die|יָ֝מ֗וּתוּ\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb wisdom|בְחָכְמָֽה׃\rb*?’[’’]
\c 5
\s1 Eliphaz Continues: God Blesses those Who Seek Him
\q1 \v 1 “\rb Call out|קְֽרָא־\rb* \rb if you please|נָ֭א\rb*,\rb |הֲיֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb but who will answer|עוֹנֶ֑ךָּ\rb*?
\q2 \rb To|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb which|מִ֖י\rb* \rb of the holy ones|מִקְּדֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb will you turn|תִּפְנֶֽה׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 2 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb resentment|כָּ֑עַשׂ\rb* \rb kills|יַהֲרָג־\rb* \rb a fool|לֶֽ֭אֱוִיל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and envy|קִנְאָֽה׃\rb* \rb slays|תָּמִ֥ית\rb* \rb the simple|וּ֝פֹתֶ֗ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb I|אֲ‍ֽנִי־\rb* \rb have seen|רָ֭אִיתִי\rb* \rb a fool|אֱוִ֣יל\rb* \rb taking root|מַשְׁרִ֑ישׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but suddenly|פִתְאֹֽם׃\rb* \rb his house|נָוֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was cursed|וָאֶקּ֖וֹב\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb His sons|בָנָ֣יו\rb* \rb are far|יִרְחֲק֣וּ\rb* \rb from safety|מִיֶּ֑שַׁע\rb*,
\q2 \rb crushed|וְיִֽדַּכְּא֥וּ\rb* \rb in court|בַ֝שַּׁ֗עַר\rb* \rb without|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb a defender|מַצִּֽיל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb The hungry|רָ֘עֵ֤ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb consume|יֹאכֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb his harvest|קְצִיר֨וֹ׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb taking it even|יִקָּחֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb from the thorns|מִצִּנִּ֥ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the thirsty|צַמִּ֣ים\rb* \rb pant after|וְשָׁאַ֖ף\rb* \rb his wealth|חֵילָֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 5:5 \ft Or \fqa and a snare snatches his wealth\f*
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֤י׀\rb* \rb distress|אָ֑וֶן\rb* \rb does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb spring|יֵצֵ֣א\rb* \rb from the dust|מֵעָפָ֣ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and trouble|עָמָֽל׃\rb* \rb does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb sprout|יִצְמַ֥ח\rb* \rb from the ground|וּ֝מֵאֲדָמָ֗ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb Yet|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb man|אָ֭דָם\rb* \rb is born|יוּלָּ֑ד\rb* \rb to trouble|לְעָמָ֣ל\rb*
\q2 \rb as surely as sparks|וּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |רֶ֝֗שֶׁף\rb* \rb fly|עֽוּף׃\rb* \rb upward|יַגְבִּ֥יהוּ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb However|אוּלָ֗ם\rb*, \rb if I were you|אֲ֭נִי\rb*, \rb I would appeal|אֶדְרֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|אֵ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and lay|אָשִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb my cause|דִּבְרָתִֽי׃\rb* \rb before|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Him|אֱ֝לֹהִ֗ים\rb*—
\q1 \v 9 \rb the One who does|עֹשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb great|גְ֭דֹלוֹת\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb unsearchable things|חֵ֑קֶר\rb*,
\q2 \rb wonders|נִ֝פְלָא֗וֹת\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb without|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb number|מִסְפָּֽר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb He gives|הַנֹּתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb rain|מָ֭טָר\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵי־\rb* \rb the earth|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and sends|וְשֹׁ֥לֵֽחַ\rb* \rb water|מַ֝יִם\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the fields|חוּצֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb He sets|לָשׂ֣וּם\rb* \rb the lowly|שְׁפָלִ֣ים\rb* \rb on high|לְמָר֑וֹם\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that mourners|וְ֝קֹדְרִ֗ים\rb* \rb are lifted|שָׂ֣גְבוּ\rb* \rb to safety|יֶֽשַׁע׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb He thwarts|מֵ֭פֵר\rb* \rb the schemes|מַחְשְׁב֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the crafty|עֲרוּמִ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that their hands|יְ֝דֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb find|תַעֲשֶׂ֥ינָה\rb* \rb no|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb success|תּוּשִׁיָּֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb He catches|לֹכֵ֣ד\rb* \rb the wise|חֲכָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb in their craftiness|בְּעָרְמָ֑ם\rb*,\f + \fr 5:13 \ft Cited in \ref 1 Corinthians 3:19|1CO 3:19\ref*\f*
\q2 \rb and sweeps away|נִמְהָֽרָה׃\rb* \rb the plans|וַעֲצַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the cunning|נִפְתָּלִ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb They encounter|יְפַגְּשׁוּ־\rb* \rb darkness|חֹ֑שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb by day|יוֹמָ֥ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and grope|יְֽמַשְׁשׁ֥וּ\rb* \rb at noon|בַֽצָּהֳרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb as in the night|וְ֝כַלַּ֗יְלָה\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb He saves|וַיֹּ֣שַׁע\rb* \rb the needy|אֶבְיֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb from the sword|מֵ֭חֶרֶב\rb* \rb in their mouth|מִפִּיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and from the clutches|וּמִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb of the powerful|חָזָ֣ק\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb So the poor|לַדַּ֣ל\rb* \rb have|וַתְּהִ֣י\rb* \rb hope|תִּקְוָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and injustice|וְ֝עֹלָ֗תָה\rb* \rb shuts|קָ֣פְצָה\rb* \rb its mouth|פִּֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb Blessed|אַשְׁרֵ֣י\rb* \rb indeed|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb is the man|אֱ֭נוֹשׁ\rb* \rb whom God|אֱל֑וֹהַּ\rb* \rb corrects|יוֹכִחֶ֣נּֽוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb so do not|אַל־\rb* \rb despise|תִּמְאָֽס׃\rb* \rb the discipline|וּמוּסַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the Almighty|שַׁ֝דַּ֗י\rb*.\f + \fr 5:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shaddai\ft ; here and throughout Job\f*
\q1 \v 18 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb wounds|יַכְאִ֣יב\rb*, \rb but He also binds|וְיֶחְבָּ֑שׁ\rb*;
\q2 \rb He strikes|יִ֝מְחַ֗ץ\rb*, \rb but His hands|וְיָדוֹ\rb* \rb also heal|תִּרְפֶּֽינָה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb He will rescue|יַצִּילֶ֑ךָּ\rb* \rb you from six|בְּשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb calamities|צָ֭רוֹת\rb*;
\q2 \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb harm|רָֽע׃\rb* \rb will touch|יִגַּ֖ע\rb* \rb you|בְּךָ֣\rb* \rb in seven|וּבְשֶׁ֓בַע׀\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb In famine|בְּ֭רָעָב\rb* \rb He will redeem you|פָּֽדְךָ֣\rb* \rb from death|מִמָּ֑וֶת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and in battle|וּ֝בְמִלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb from the stroke|מִ֣ידֵי\rb* \rb of the sword|חָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb You will be hidden|תֵּחָבֵ֑א\rb* \rb from the scourge|בְּשׁ֣וֹט\rb* \rb of the tongue|לָ֭שׁוֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and will not|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb fear|תִירָ֥א\rb* \rb havoc|מִ֝שֹּׁ֗ד\rb* \rb when|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it comes|יָבֽוֹא׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb You will laugh|תִּשְׂחָ֑ק\rb* \rb at destruction|לְשֹׁ֣ד\rb* \rb and famine|וּלְכָפָ֣ן\rb*,
