\c 7
\s1 Job Continues: Life Seems Futile
\q1 \v 1 “\rb Is not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb man|לֶאֱנ֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb consigned to labor|צָבָ֣א\rb* \rb on|עַל\rb* \rb earth|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*?
\q2 \rb Are not his days|וְכִימֵ֖י\rb* \rb like those|יָמָֽיו׃\rb* \rb of a hired hand|שָׂכִ֣יר\rb*?
\q1 \v 2 \rb Like a slave|כְּעֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb he longs for|יִשְׁאַף־\rb* \rb shade|צֵ֑ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb like a hireling|וּ֝כְשָׂכִ֗יר\rb* \rb he waits for|יְקַוֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb his wages|פָעֳלֽוֹ׃\rb*.
