\q2 \rb and nights|וְלֵיל֥וֹת\rb* \rb of misery|עָ֝מָ֗ל\rb* \rb are appointed|מִנּוּ־\rb* \rb to me|לִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb When|אִם־\rb* \rb I lie down|שָׁכַ֗בְתִּי\rb* \rb I think|וְאָמַ֗רְתִּי\rb*:
\q2 ‘\rb When|מָתַ֣י\rb* \rb will I get up|אָ֭קוּם\rb*?’
\q1 \rb But the night|עָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb drags on|וּמִדַּד־\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I toss and turn|וְשָׂבַ֖עְתִּי\rb*\rb |נְדֻדִ֣ים\rb* \rb until|עֲדֵי־\rb* \rb dawn|נָֽשֶׁף׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb My flesh|בְּשָׂרִ֣י\rb* \rb is clothed|לָ֘בַ֤שׁ\rb* \rb with worms|רִ֭מָּה\rb*
\q2 \rb and encrusted|וְגִישׁ\rb* \rb with dirt|עָפָ֑ר\rb*;
\q2 \rb my skin|עוֹרִ֥י\rb* \rb is cracked|רָ֝גַ֗ע\rb* \rb and festering|וַיִּמָּאֵֽס׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb My days|יָמַ֣י\rb* \rb are swifter|קַ֭לּוּ\rb* \rb than|מִנִּי־\rb* \rb a weaver’s shuttle|אָ֑רֶג\rb*;
\q2 \rb they come to an end|וַ֝יִּכְל֗וּ\rb* \rb without|בְּאֶ֣פֶס\rb* \rb hope|תִּקְוָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb Remember|זְ֭כֹר\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb my life|חַיָּ֑י\rb* \rb is but a breath|ר֣וּחַ\rb*.
\q2 \rb My eyes|עֵ֝ינִ֗י\rb* \rb will never|לֹא־\rb* \rb again|תָשׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb see|לִרְא֥וֹת\rb* \rb happiness|טֽוֹב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb The eye|עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb that beholds me|רֹ֑אִי\rb* \rb will no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer see me|תְ֭שׁוּרֵנִי\rb*.
\q2 \rb You will look|עֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb for me|בִּ֣י\rb*, \rb but I will be no more|וְאֵינֶֽנִּי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb As a cloud|עָ֭נָן\rb* \rb vanishes|כָּלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and is gone|וַיֵּלַ֑ךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb so|כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb he who goes down|יוֹרֵ֥ד\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁ֝א֗וֹל\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb come back up|יַעֲלֶֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb He never|לֹא־\rb*\rb |ע֣וֹד\rb* \rb returns|יָשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb to his house|לְבֵית֑וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb his place|מְקֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb remembers him|יַכִּירֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb no more|ע֣וֹד\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Therefore|גַּם־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֮\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb restrain|אֶחֱשָׂ֫ךְ\rb* \rb my mouth|פִּ֥י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will speak|אֲ‍ֽ֭דַבְּרָה\rb* \rb in the anguish|בְּצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of my spirit|רוּחִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will complain|אָ֝שִׂ֗יחָה\rb* \rb in the bitterness|בְּמַ֣ר\rb* \rb of my soul|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb Am I|אָ֭נִי\rb* \rb the sea|הֲ‍ֽיָם־\rb*, \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb the monster of the deep|תַּנִּ֑ין\rb*,
\q2 \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You must keep me under|תָשִׂ֖ים\rb*\rb |עָלַ֣י\rb* \rb guard|מִשְׁמָֽר׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 13 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I think|אָ֭מַרְתִּי\rb* \rb my bed|עַרְשִׂ֑י\rb* \rb will comfort me|תְּנַחֲמֵ֣נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and my couch|מִשְׁכָּבִֽי׃\rb* \rb will ease|יִשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb my complaint|בְ֝שִׂיחִ֗י\rb*,
\q1 \v 14 \rb then You frighten me|וְחִתַּתַּ֥נִי\rb* \rb with dreams|בַחֲלֹמ֑וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb and terrify me|תְּבַעֲתַֽנִּי׃\rb* \rb with visions|וּֽמֵחֶזְיֹנ֥וֹת\rb*,
\q1 \v 15 \rb so that I|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb would prefer|וַתִּבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb strangling|מַחֲנָ֣ק\rb* \rb and death|מָ֝֗וֶת\rb*
\q2 \rb over my life in this body|מֵֽעַצְמוֹתָֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb I loathe my life|מָ֭אַסְתִּי\rb*! \rb I would not|לֹא־\rb* \rb live|אֶֽחְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb forever|לְעֹלָ֣ם\rb*.
\q2 \rb Leave me alone|חֲדַ֥ל\rb*\rb |מִ֝מֶּ֗נִּי\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb my days are|יָמָֽי׃\rb* \rb but a breath|הֶ֥בֶל\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb What|מָֽה־\rb* \rb is man|אֱ֭נוֹשׁ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb You should exalt him|תְגַדְּלֶ֑נּוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb that|וְכִי־\rb* \rb You should set|תָשִׁ֖ית\rb* \rb Your heart|לִבֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb upon him|אֵלָ֣יו\rb*,
\q1 \v 18 \rb that You attend to him|וַתִּפְקְדֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb every morning|לִבְקָרִ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and test him|תִּבְחָנֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb every moment|לִ֝רְגָעִ֗ים\rb*?
\q1 \v 19 \rb Will You never|כַּ֭מָּה\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb look away|תִשְׁעֶ֣ה\rb* \rb from me|מִמֶּ֑נִּי\rb*,
\q2 \rb or|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb leave me alone|תַ֝רְפֵּ֗נִי\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb swallow|בִּלְעִ֥י\rb* \rb my spittle|רֻקִּֽי׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 20 \rb If I have sinned|חָטָ֡אתִי\rb*, \rb what|מָ֤ה\rb* \rb have I done|אֶפְעַ֨ל׀\rb* \rb to You|לָךְ֮\rb*,
\q2 \rb O watcher|נֹצֵ֪ר\rb* \rb of mankind|הָאָ֫דָ֥ם\rb*?
\q1 \rb Why|לָ֤מָה\rb* \rb have You made me|שַׂמְתַּ֣נִי\rb* \rb Your|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb target|לְמִפְגָּ֣ע\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that I am|וָאֶהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb a burden|לְמַשָּֽׂא׃\rb* \rb to You|עָלַ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 7:20 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa to myself\f*?
\q1 \v 21 \rb Why|וּמֶ֤ה׀\rb* \rb do You not|לֹא־\rb* \rb pardon|תִשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb my transgression|פִשְׁעִי֮\rb*
\q2 \rb and take away|וְתַעֲבִ֪יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my iniquity|עֲוֺ֫נִ֥י\rb*?
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb soon|עַ֭תָּה\rb* \rb I will lie down|אֶשְׁכָּ֑ב\rb* \rb in the dust|לֶעָפָ֣ר\rb*;
\q2 \rb You will seek me|וְשִׁ֖חֲרְתַּ֣נִי\rb*, \rb but I will be no more|וְאֵינֶֽנִּי׃פ\rb*.”
\c 8
\s1 Bildad: Job Should Repent
\p \v 1 \rb Then Bildad|בִּלְדַּ֥ד\rb* \rb the Shuhite|הַשּׁוּחִ֗י\rb*\rb |וַיֹאמַֽר׃\rb* \rb replied|וַ֭יַּעַן\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |אָ֥ן\rb* \rb will you go on saying|תְּמַלֶּל־\rb* \rb such things|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb*?
\q2 \rb The words|אִמְרֵי־\rb* \rb of your mouth|פִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb are a blustering|כַּ֝בִּיר\rb* \rb wind|וְר֥וּחַ\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb Does God|הַ֭אֵל\rb* \rb pervert|יְעַוֵּ֣ת\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb*?
\q2 \rb |וְאִם־\rb* \rb Does the Almighty|שַׁ֝דַּ֗י\rb* \rb pervert|יְעַוֵּֽת־\rb* \rb what is right|צֶֽדֶק׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 4 \rb When|אִם־\rb* \rb your children|בָּנֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb sinned|חָֽטְאוּ־\rb* \rb against Him|ל֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb He gave them over|וַֽ֝יְשַׁלְּחֵ֗ם\rb*\rb |בְּיַד־\rb* \rb to their rebellion|פִּשְׁעָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb But if|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַ֭תָּה\rb* \rb would earnestly seek|תְּשַׁחֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb God|אֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb*
\q2 \rb and ask the Almighty|שַׁ֝דַּ֗י\rb* \rb for mercy|תִּתְחַנָּֽן׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 6 \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אָ֥תָּה\rb* \rb are pure|זַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and upright|וְיָשָׁ֗ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb even|כִּי־\rb* \rb now|עַ֭תָּה\rb* \rb He will rouse Himself|יָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb on your behalf|עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and restore|וְ֝שִׁלַּ֗ם\rb* \rb your righteous|צִדְקֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb estate|נְוַ֣ת\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb Though your beginnings|רֵאשִׁיתְךָ֣\rb* \rb were|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb modest|מִצְעָ֑ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb your latter days|וְ֝אַחֲרִיתְךָ֗\rb* \rb will flourish|יִשְׂגֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Please|נָ֭א\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb inquire|שְׁאַל־\rb* \rb of past|רִישׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb generations|לְדֹ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and consider|וְ֝כוֹנֵ֗ן\rb* \rb the discoveries|לְחֵ֣קֶר\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we were born|אֲ֭נַחְנוּ\rb* \rb yesterday|תְמ֣וֹל\rb* \rb and know|נֵדָ֑ע\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb nothing|וְלֹ֣א\rb*;
\q2 \rb our days|יָמֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵי־\rb* \rb earth|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb are but a shadow|צֵ֖ל\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Will they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb teach you|י֭וֹרוּךָ\rb* \rb and tell|יֹ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and speak|יוֹצִ֥אוּ\rb*\rb |מִלִּֽים׃\rb* \rb from their understanding|וּ֝מִלִּבָּ֗ם\rb*?
\q1 \v 11 \rb Does papyrus|גֹּ֭מֶא\rb* \rb grow|הֲיִֽגְאֶה־\rb* \rb where there is no|בְּלֹ֣א\rb* \rb marsh|בִצָּ֑ה\rb*?
\q2 \rb Do reeds|אָ֥חוּ\rb* \rb flourish|יִשְׂגֶּה־\rb* \rb without|בְלִי־\rb* \rb water|מָֽיִם׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 12 \rb While|עֹדֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb the shoots|בְ֭אִבּוֹ\rb* \rb are still uncut|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יִקָּטֵ֑ף\rb*,
\q2 \rb they dry up|יִיבָֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb more quickly than|וְלִפְנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |כָל־\rb* \rb grass|חָצִ֣יר\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Such|כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb is the destiny|אָ֭רְחוֹת\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who forget|שֹׁ֣כְחֵי\rb* \rb God|אֵ֑ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb so the hope|וְתִקְוַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the godless|חָנֵ֣ף\rb* \rb will perish|תֹּאבֵֽד׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb His|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb confidence|כִּסְל֑וֹ\rb* \rb is fragile|יָק֥וֹט\rb*;
\q2 \rb his security|מִבְטַחֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb is in a spider’s|עַ֝כָּבִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb web|וּבֵ֥ית\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb He leans|יִשָּׁעֵ֣ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his web|בֵּ֭יתוֹ\rb*,\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb but it gives way|יַעֲמֹ֑ד\rb*;
\q2 \rb he holds fast|יַחֲזִ֥יק\rb*, \rb but it does not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb endure|יָקֽוּם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb He|ה֭וּא\rb* \rb is a well-watered plant|רָטֹ֣ב\rb* \rb in|לִפְנֵי־\rb* \rb the sunshine|שָׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb spreading|תֵצֵֽא׃\rb* \rb its shoots|יֹֽנַקְתּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb over|וְעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the garden|גַּ֝נָּת֗וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb His roots|שָֽׁרָשָׁ֣יו\rb* \rb wrap|יְסֻבָּ֑כוּ\rb* \rb around|עַל־\rb* \rb the rock heap|גַּ֭ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb he looks for|יֶחֱזֶֽה׃\rb* \rb a home among|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb the stones|אֲבָנִ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb he is uprooted|יְבַלְּעֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb from his place|מִמְּקוֹמ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb it will disown|וְכִ֥חֶשׁ\rb* \rb him|בּ֝֗וֹ\rb*, \rb saying, ‘ I never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb saw you|רְאִיתִֽיךָ׃\rb*.’
\q1 \v 19 \rb Surely|הֶן־\rb* \rb this|ה֭וּא\rb* \rb is the joy|מְשׂ֣וֹשׂ\rb* \rb of his way|דַּרְכּ֑וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb yet others|אַחֵ֥ר\rb* \rb will spring|יִצְמָֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb from the dust|וּ֝מֵעָפָ֗ר\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb Behold|הֶן־\rb*, \rb God|אֵ֭ל\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb reject|יִמְאַס־\rb* \rb the blameless|תָּ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb nor will He|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb strengthen|יַ֝חֲזִ֗יק\rb* \rb the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of evildoers|מְרֵעִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb He will yet|עַד־\rb* \rb fill your mouth|פִּ֑יךָ\rb* \rb with|יְמַלֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb laughter|שְׂח֣וֹק\rb*,
\q2 \rb and your lips|וּשְׂפָתֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb with a shout of joy|תְרוּעָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb Your enemies|שֹׂנְאֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb will be clothed|יִלְבְּשׁוּ־\rb* \rb in shame|בֹ֑שֶׁת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the tent|וְאֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb will be no more|אֵינֶֽנּוּ׃פ\rb*.”
\c 9
\s1 Job: How Can I Contend with God?
\p \v 1 \rb Then Job|אִיּ֗וֹב\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb Yes|אָ֭מְנָם\rb*, \rb I know|יָדַ֣עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִי־\rb* \rb it is so|כֵ֑ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb but how|וּמַה־\rb* \rb can a mortal|אֱנ֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb be righteous|יִּצְדַּ֖ק\rb* \rb before|עִם־\rb* \rb God|אֵֽל׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 3 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb one wished|יַ֭חְפֹּץ\rb* \rb to contend|לָרִ֣יב\rb* \rb with God|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 9:3 \ft Or \fqa If God wished to contend with someone\f*
\q2 \rb he could not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb answer Him|יַ֝עֲנֶ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb one time|אַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb out of|מִנִּי־\rb* \rb a thousand|אָֽלֶף׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb God is wise|חֲכַ֣ם\rb* \rb in heart|לֵ֭בָב\rb* \rb and mighty|וְאַמִּ֣יץ\rb* \rb in strength|כֹּ֑חַ\rb*.
\q2 \rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb has resisted|הִקְשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb Him|אֵ֝לָ֗יו\rb* \rb and prospered|וַיִּשְׁלָֽם׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 5 \rb He moves|הַמַּעְתִּ֣יק\rb* \rb mountains|הָ֭רִים\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb their knowledge|יָדָ֑עוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb overturns them|הֲפָכָ֣ם\rb* \rb in His anger|בְּאַפּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb He shakes|הַמַּרְגִּ֣יז\rb* \rb the earth|אֶ֭רֶץ\rb* \rb from its place|מִמְּקוֹמָ֑הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that its foundations|וְ֝עַמּוּדֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb tremble|יִתְפַלָּצֽוּן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb He commands|הָאֹמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb the sun|לַ֭חֶרֶס\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to shine|יִזְרָ֑ח\rb*;\f + \fr 9:7 \ft Or \fqa rise\f*
\q2 \rb He seals off|וּבְעַ֖ד\rb*\rb |יַחְתֹּֽם׃\rb* \rb the stars|כּוֹכָבִ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb He alone|לְבַדּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb stretches out|נֹטֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the heavens|שָׁמַ֣יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and treads|וְ֝דוֹרֵ֗ךְ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the waves|בָּ֥מֳתֵי\rb* \rb of the sea|יָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb He is the Maker|עֹֽשֶׂה־\rb* \rb of the Bear|עָ֭שׁ\rb* \rb and Orion|כְּסִ֥יל\rb*,
\q2 \rb of the Pleiades|וְכִימָ֗ה\rb* \rb and the constellations|וְחַדְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the south|תֵמָֽן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb He does|עֹשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb great things|גְ֭דֹלוֹת\rb* \rb beyond|עַד־\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb searching out|חֵ֑קֶר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and wonders|וְנִפְלָא֗וֹת\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb without|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb number|מִסְפָּֽר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb Were He|הֵ֤ן\rb* \rb to pass|יַעֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb by me|עָ֭לַי\rb*, \rb I would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb see Him|אֶרְאֶ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb were He to move|וְ֝יַחֲלֹ֗ף\rb*, \rb I would not|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb recognize|אָבִ֥ין\rb* \rb Him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb If|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb He takes away|יַ֭חְתֹּף\rb*,\f + \fr 9:12 \ft Or \fqa snatches someone in death\f* \rb who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb can stop Him|יְשִׁיבֶ֑נּוּ\rb*?
\q2 \rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb dares to ask|יֹאמַ֥ר\rb* \rb Him|אֵ֝לָ֗יו\rb*, ‘\rb What|מַֽה־\rb* \rb are You doing|תַּעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb*?’
\q1 \v 13 \rb God|אֱ֭לוֹהַּ\rb* \rb does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb restrain|יָשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb His anger|אַפּ֑וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb the helpers|עֹ֣זְרֵי\rb* \rb of Rahab|רָֽהַב׃\rb* \rb cower|שָׁ֝חֲח֗וּ\rb* \rb beneath Him|תַּחַתוֹ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb How|אַ֭ף\rb* \rb then|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb can I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb answer Him|אֶֽעֱנֶ֑נּוּ\rb*
