\q2 \rb who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb can summon Him|יוֹעִידֵֽנִי׃\rb*\f + \fr 9:19 \ft See LXX; Hebrew \fqa me\f*?
\q1 \v 20 \rb Even if|אִם־\rb* \rb I were righteous|אֶ֭צְדָּק\rb*, \rb my mouth|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb would condemn me|יַרְשִׁיעֵ֑נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb if I|אָ֝֗נִי\rb* \rb were blameless|תָּֽם־\rb*, \rb it would declare me guilty|וַֽיַּעְקְשֵֽׁנִי׃\rb*.\f + \fr 9:20 \ft Or \fqa He would declare me guilty\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Though I|אָ֭נִי\rb* \rb am blameless|תָּֽם־\rb*, \rb I have no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb concern|אֵדַ֥ע\rb* \rb for myself|נַפְשִׁ֗י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I despise|אֶמְאַ֥ס\rb* \rb my own life|חַיָּֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb It|הִ֥יא\rb* \rb is all the same|אַחַ֗ת\rb*, \rb and so|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb I say|אָמַ֑רְתִּי\rb*,
\q2 ‘\rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb destroys|מְכַלֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb both the blameless|תָּ֥ם\rb* \rb and the wicked|וְ֝רָשָׁ֗ע\rb*.’
\q1 \v 23 \rb When|אִם־\rb* \rb the scourge|שׁ֭וֹט\rb* \rb brings sudden|פִּתְאֹ֑ם\rb* \rb death|יָמִ֣ית\rb*,
\q2 \rb He mocks|יִלְעָֽג׃\rb* \rb the despair|לְמַסַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of the innocent|נְקִיִּ֣ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb The earth|אֶ֤רֶץ׀\rb* \rb is given|נִתְּנָ֬ה\rb* \rb into the hand|בְֽיַד־\rb* \rb of the wicked|רָשָׁ֗ע\rb*;
\q2 \rb He blindfolds|פְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יְכַסֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb its judges|שֹׁפְטֶ֥יהָ\rb*.
\q2 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb it is not He|לֹ֖א\rb*, \rb then|אֵפ֣וֹא\rb* \rb who|מִי־\rb* \rb is it|הֽוּא׃\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 25 \rb My days|וְיָמַ֣י\rb* \rb are swifter|קַ֭לּוּ\rb* \rb than|מִנִּי־\rb* \rb a runner|רָ֑ץ\rb*;
\q2 \rb they flee|בָּֽ֝רְח֗וּ\rb* \rb without|לֹא־\rb* \rb seeing|רָא֥וּ\rb* \rb good|טוֹבָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb They sweep by|חָ֭לְפוּ\rb* \rb like|עִם־\rb* \rb boats|אֳנִיּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of papyrus|אֵבֶ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb like an eagle|כְּ֝נֶ֗שֶׁר\rb* \rb swooping down|יָט֥וּשׂ\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵי־\rb* \rb its prey|אֹֽכֶל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I were to say|אָ֭מְרִי\rb*, ‘\rb I will forget|אֶשְׁכְּחָ֣ה\rb* \rb my complaint|שִׂיחִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and change|אֶעֶזְבָ֖ה\rb* \rb my expression|פָנַ֣י\rb* \rb and smile|וְאַבְלִֽיגָה׃\rb*,’
\q1 \v 28 \rb I would still dread|יָגֹ֥רְתִּי\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb my sufferings|עַצְּבֹתָ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I know|יָ֝דַ֗עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb You will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb acquit me|תְנַקֵּֽנִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 29 \rb Since I am|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb already found guilty|אֶרְשָׁ֑ע\rb*,
\q2 \rb why|לָמָּה־\rb*\rb |זֶּ֝֗ה\rb* \rb should I labor|אִיגָֽע׃\rb* \rb in vain|הֶ֣בֶל\rb*?
\q1 \v 30 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I should wash|הִתְרָחַ֥צְתִּי\rb* \rb myself|בְמוֹ\rb* \rb with snow|שָׁ֑לֶג\rb*\f + \fr 9:30 \ft Or \fqa soap\f*
\q2 \rb and cleanse|וַ֝הֲזִכּ֗וֹתִי\rb* \rb my hands|כַּפָּֽי׃\rb* \rb with lye|בְּבֹ֣ר\rb*,
\q1 \v 31 \rb then|אָ֭ז\rb* \rb You would plunge me|תִּטְבְּלֵ֑נִי\rb* \rb into the pit|בַּשַּׁ֣חַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and even my own clothes|שַׂלְמוֹתָֽי׃\rb* \rb would despise me|וְ֝תִֽעֲב֗וּנִי\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 32 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb He is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb like me|כָּמֹ֣נִי\rb*, \rb that I can answer Him|אֶֽעֱנֶ֑נּוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb that we can take|נָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb each other|יַ֝חְדָּ֗ו\rb* \rb to court|בַּמִּשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 33 \rb Nor|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb is there|יֵשׁ־\rb* \rb a mediator|מוֹכִ֑יחַ\rb* \rb between us|בֵּינֵ֣ינוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb to lay|יָשֵׁ֖ת\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֣וֹ\rb* \rb upon us|עַל־\rb* \rb both|שְׁנֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 34 \rb Let Him remove|יָסֵ֣ר\rb* \rb His rod|שִׁבְט֑וֹ\rb* \rb from me|מֵעָלַ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that His terror|וְ֝אֵמָת֗וֹ\rb* \rb will no|אַֽל־\rb* \rb longer frighten me|תְּבַעֲתַֽנִּי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 35 \rb Then I would speak|אַֽ֭דַבְּרָה\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb fear of Him|אִירָאֶ֑נּוּ\rb*.
\q2 \rb But|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb as it is|לֹא־\rb*\rb |כֵ֥ן\rb*, \rb I|אָ֝נֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb am on my own|עִמָּדִֽי׃\rb*.[’’]
\c 10
\s1 Job’s Plea to God
\q1 \v 1 “\rb I loathe|נָֽקְטָ֥ה\rb* \rb my own|נַפְשִׁ֗י\rb* \rb life|בְּחַ֫יָּ֥י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will express|אֶֽעֶזְבָ֣ה\rb*\rb |עָלַ֣י\rb* \rb my complaint|שִׂיחִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and speak|אֲ֝דַבְּרָה֗\rb* \rb in the bitterness|בְּמַ֣ר\rb* \rb of my soul|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb I will say|אֹמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|אֱ֭לוֹהַּ\rb*:
\q2 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb condemn me|תַּרְשִׁיעֵ֑נִי\rb*!
\q2 \rb Let me know|הֽ֝וֹדִיעֵ֗נִי\rb* \rb why|עַ֣ל\rb*\rb |מַה־\rb* \rb You prosecute me|תְּרִיבֵֽנִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb Does it please|הֲט֤וֹב\rb* \rb You|לְךָ֨׀\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb to oppress me|תַעֲשֹׁ֗ק\rb*,\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*
\q2 \rb to reject|תִ֭מְאַס\rb* \rb the work|יְגִ֣יעַ\rb* \rb of Your hands|כַּפֶּ֑יךָ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb*
\q2 \rb and favor|הוֹפָֽעְתָּ׃\rb* \rb the schemes|עֲצַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb*?
\q1 \v 4 \rb Do You have eyes|הַעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of flesh|בָשָׂ֣ר\rb*?
\q2 \rb |אִם־\rb* \rb Do You see|כִּרְא֖וֹת\rb* \rb as man|אֱנ֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb sees|תִּרְאֶֽה׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 5 \rb Are Your days|הֲכִימֵ֣י\rb* \rb like those|יָמֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb of a mortal|אֱנ֣וֹשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb Your years|שְׁ֝נוֹתֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb like those|כִּ֣ימֵי\rb* \rb of a man|גָֽבֶר׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 6 \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You should seek|תְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb my iniquity|לַעֲוֺנִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and search out|תִדְרֽוֹשׁ׃\rb* \rb my sin|וּ֭לְחַטָּאתִ֥י\rb* —
\q1 \v 7 \rb though|עַֽל־\rb* \rb You know|דַּ֭עְתְּךָ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I am not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb guilty|אֶרְשָׁ֑ע\rb*,
\q2 \rb and there is no|וְאֵ֖ין\rb* \rb deliverance|מַצִּֽיל׃\rb* \rb from Your hand|מִיָּדְךָ֣\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Your hands|יָדֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb shaped me|עִ֭צְּבוּנִי\rb* \rb and altogether|יַ֥חַד\rb* \rb formed me|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֑וּנִי\rb*.
\q2 \rb Would You now turn|סָ֝בִ֗יב\rb* \rb and destroy me|וַֽתְּבַלְּעֵֽנִי׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 9 \rb Please|נָ֭א\rb* \rb remember|זְכָר־\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb You molded me|עֲשִׂיתָ֑נִי\rb* \rb like clay|כַחֹ֣מֶר\rb*.
\q2 \rb Would You now return me|תְּשִׁיבֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb to|וְֽאֶל־\rb* \rb dust|עָפָ֥ר\rb*?
\q1 \v 10 \rb Did You not|הֲלֹ֣א\rb* \rb pour me out|תַּתִּיכֵ֑נִי\rb* \rb like milk|כֶ֭חָלָב\rb*,
\q2 \rb and curdle me|תַּקְפִּיאֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb like cheese|וְ֝כַגְּבִנָּ֗ה\rb*?
\q1 \v 11 \rb You clothed me|תַּלְבִּישֵׁ֑נִי\rb* \rb with skin|ע֣וֹר\rb* \rb and flesh|וּ֭בָשָׂר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and knit me together|תְּסֹכְכֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb with bones|וּֽבַעֲצָמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb and sinews|וְ֝גִידִ֗ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb You have granted|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb me|עִמָּדִ֑י\rb* \rb life|חַיִּ֣ים\rb* \rb and loving devotion|וָ֭חֶסֶד\rb*,\f + \fr 10:12 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f*
\q2 \rb and Your care|וּ֝פְקֻדָּתְךָ֗\rb* \rb has preserved|שָֽׁמְרָ֥ה\rb* \rb my spirit|רוּחִֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Yet You concealed|צָפַ֣נְתָּ\rb* \rb these things|וְ֭אֵלֶּה\rb* \rb in Your heart|בִלְבָבֶ֑ךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I know|יָ֝דַ֗עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb this was|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb in Your mind|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*:
\q1 \v 14 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I sinned|חָטָ֥אתִי\rb*, \rb You would take note|וּשְׁמַרְתָּ֑נִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and would not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb acquit me|תְנַקֵּֽנִי׃\rb* \rb of my iniquity|וּ֝מֵעֲוֺנִ֗י\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I am guilty|רָשַׁ֡עְתִּי\rb*, \rb woe|אַלְלַ֬י\rb* \rb to me|לִ֗י\rb*!
\q2 \rb And even if I am righteous|וְ֭צָדַקְתִּי\rb*, \rb I cannot|לֹא־\rb* \rb lift|אֶשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb my head|רֹאשִׁ֑י\rb*.
\q1 \rb I am full|שְׂבַ֥ע\rb* \rb of shame|קָ֝ל֗וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb and aware of|וּרְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb my affliction|עָנְיִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb Should I hold my head high|וְ֭יִגְאֶה\rb*,
\q2 \rb You would hunt me|תְּצוּדֵ֑נִי\rb* \rb like a lion|כַּשַּׁ֣חַל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and again|וְ֝תָשֹׁ֗ב\rb* \rb display Your power|תִּתְפַּלָּא־\rb* \rb against me|בִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb You produce new|תְּחַדֵּ֬שׁ\rb* \rb witnesses|עֵדֶ֨יךָ׀\rb* \rb against me|נֶגְדִּ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb and multiply|וְתֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb Your anger|כַּֽ֭עַשְׂךָ\rb* \rb toward me|עִמָּדִ֑י\rb*.
\q1 \rb Hardships|וְצָבָ֣א\rb* \rb assault me|עִמִּֽי׃\rb*
\q2 \rb in wave after wave|חֲלִיפ֖וֹת\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb Why then|וְלָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb did You bring me|הֹצֵאתָ֑נִי\rb* \rb from the womb|מֵ֭רֶחֶם\rb*?
\q2 \rb Oh, that I had died|אֶ֝גְוַ֗ע\rb*, \rb and no|לֹא־\rb* \rb eye|וְעַ֣יִן\rb* \rb had seen me|תִרְאֵֽנִי׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 19 \rb If only|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I had never|לֹא־\rb* \rb come|הָיִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb to be|אֶהְיֶ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but had been carried|אוּבָֽל׃\rb* \rb from the womb|מִ֝בֶּ֗טֶן\rb* \rb to the grave|לַקֶּ֥בֶר\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb Are my days|יָמַ֣י\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb few|מְעַ֣ט\rb*?
\q2 \rb Withdraw|יֶחְדָּל\rb*\rb |יָשִׁית\rb* \rb from me|מִ֝מֶּ֗נִּי\rb*, \rb that I may have a little comfort|וְאַבְלִ֥יגָה\rb*,
\q1 \v 21 \rb before|בְּטֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb I go|אֵ֭לֵךְ\rb* — \rb never|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to return|אָשׁ֑וּב\rb* —
\q2 \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of darkness|חֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb and gloom|וְצַלְמָֽוֶת׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 22 \rb to a land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of utter darkness|עֵיפָ֨תָה׀\rb*\rb |כְּמ֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֹ֗פֶל\rb*,
\q2 \rb of deep shadow|צַ֭לְמָוֶת\rb* \rb and disorder|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |סְדָרִ֗ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb where even the light|וַתֹּ֥פַע\rb* \rb is like|כְּמוֹ־\rb* \rb darkness|אֹֽפֶל׃פ\rb*.”
\c 11
\s1 Zophar Rebukes Job
\p \v 1 \rb Then Zophar|צֹפַ֥ר\rb* \rb the Naamathite|הַֽנַּעֲמָתִ֗י\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb* \rb replied|וַ֭יַּעַן\rb*:
