\q1 \v 20 \rb Those in the west|אַחֲרֹנִ֑ים\rb* \rb are appalled|נָשַׁ֣מּוּ\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb his fate|י֭וֹמוֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb while those in the east|וְ֝קַדְמֹנִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אָ֣חֲזוּ\rb* \rb tremble in horror|שָֽׂעַר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb Surely|אַךְ־\rb* \rb such|אֵ֭לֶּה\rb* \rb is the dwelling|מִשְׁכְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the wicked|עַוָּ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and|וְ֝זֶ֗ה\rb* \rb the place|מְק֣וֹם\rb* \rb of one who does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb know|יָדַֽע־\rb* \rb God|אֵֽל׃ס\rb*.”
\c 19
\s1 Job: My Redeemer Lives
\p \v 1 \rb Then Job|אִיּ֗וֹב\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |אָ֭נָה\rb* \rb will you torment|תּוֹגְי֣וּן\rb* \rb me|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and crush me|וּֽתְדַכְּאוּנַ֥נִי\rb* \rb with your words|בְמִלִּֽים׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 3 \rb Ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb times|פְּ֭עָמִים\rb* \rb now|זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb you have reproached me|תַּכְלִימ֑וּנִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb you shamelessly|תֵ֝בֹ֗שׁוּ\rb* \rb mistreat|תַּהְכְּרוּ־\rb* \rb me|לִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb Even if|וְאַף־\rb*\rb |אָמְנָ֥ם\rb* \rb I have truly gone astray|שָׁגִ֑יתִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb my error|מְשׁוּגָתִֽי׃\rb* \rb concerns me|תָּלִ֥ין\rb* \rb alone|אִ֝תִּ֗י\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb indeed|אָ֭מְנָם\rb* \rb you would exalt yourselves|תַּגְדִּ֑ילוּ\rb* \rb above me|עָלַ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb and use my disgrace|חֶרְפָּתִּֽי׃\rb*\rb |וְתוֹכִ֥יחוּ\rb* \rb against me|עָ֝לַ֗י\rb*,
\q1 \v 6 \rb then|אֵ֭פוֹ\rb* \rb understand|דְּֽעוּ־\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb it is God|אֱל֣וֹהַּ\rb* \rb who has wronged me|עִוְּתָ֑נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and drawn His net|וּ֝מְצוּד֗וֹ\rb* \rb around|הִקִּֽיף׃\rb* \rb me|עָלַ֥י\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb Though|הֵ֤ן\rb* \rb I cry out|אֶצְעַ֣ק\rb*, ‘\rb Violence|חָ֭מָס\rb*!’ \rb I get no|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb response|אֵעָנֶ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb though I call for help|אֲ֝שַׁוַּ֗ע\rb*, \rb there is no|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb He has blocked|גָ֭דַר\rb* \rb my way|אָרְחִ֣י\rb* \rb so I cannot|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb pass|אֶעֱב֑וֹר\rb*;
\q2 \rb He has veiled|וְעַ֥ל\rb*\rb |יָשִֽׂים׃\rb* \rb my paths|נְ֝תִיבוֹתַ֗י\rb* \rb with darkness|חֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb He has stripped me|הִפְשִׁ֑יט\rb* \rb of my honor|כְּ֭בוֹדִי\rb*\rb |מֵעָלַ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb and removed|וַ֝יָּ֗סַר\rb* \rb the crown|עֲטֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb from my head|רֹאשִֽׁי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb He tears me down|יִתְּצֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb on every side|סָ֭בִיב\rb* \rb until I am gone|וָאֵלַ֑ךְ\rb*;
\q2 \rb He uproots|וַיַּסַּ֥ע\rb* \rb my hope|תִּקְוָתִֽי׃\rb* \rb like a tree|כָּ֝עֵ֗ץ\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb His anger|אַפּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb burns|וַיַּ֣חַר\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and He counts me|וַיַּחְשְׁבֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb among His enemies|כְצָרָֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb His troops|גְדוּדָ֗יו\rb* \rb advance|יָ֘בֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb together|יַ֤חַד׀\rb*;
\q2 \rb they construct|וַיָּסֹ֣לּוּ\rb* \rb a ramp|דַּרְכָּ֑ם\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb and encamp|וַיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֣יב\rb* \rb my tent|לְאָהֳלִֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb He has removed|הִרְחִ֑יק\rb* \rb my brothers|אַ֭חַי\rb* \rb from me|מֵעָלַ֣י\rb*;
\q2 \rb my acquaintances|וְ֝יֹדְעַ֗י\rb*\rb |אַךְ־\rb* \rb have abandoned|זָ֥רוּ\rb* \rb me|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb My kinsmen|קְרוֹבָ֑י\rb* \rb have failed me|חָדְל֥וּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my friends|וּֽמְיֻדָּעַ֥י\rb* \rb have forgotten me|שְׁכֵחֽוּנִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb My guests|בֵיתִ֣י\rb* \rb and maidservants|וְ֭אַמְהֹתַי\rb* \rb count me|תַּחְשְׁבֻ֑נִי\rb* \rb as a stranger|לְזָ֣ר\rb*;
\q2 \rb I am|הָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb a foreigner|נָ֝כְרִ֗י\rb* \rb in their sight|בְעֵינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb I call|קָ֭רָאתִי\rb* \rb for my servant|לְעַבְדִּ֣י\rb*, \rb but he does not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb answer|יַעֲנֶ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb though I implore|אֶתְחַנֶּן־\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb with|בְּמוֹ־\rb* \rb my own mouth|פִ֝֗י\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb My breath|ר֭וּחִֽי\rb* \rb is repulsive|זָ֣רָה\rb* \rb to my wife|לְאִשְׁתִּ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I am loathsome|וְ֝חַנֹּתִ֗י\rb* \rb to my own family|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |בִטְנִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb Even|גַּם־\rb* \rb little boys|עֲ֭וִילִים\rb* \rb scorn|מָ֣אֲסוּ\rb* \rb me|בִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb when I appear|אָ֝ק֗וּמָה\rb*, \rb they deride|וַיְדַבְּרוּ־\rb* \rb me|בִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb my best friends|מְתֵ֣י\rb*\rb |סוֹדִ֑י\rb* \rb despise me|תִּֽ֭עֲבוּנִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and those|וְזֶֽה־\rb* \rb I love|אָ֝הַ֗בְתִּי\rb* \rb have turned|נֶהְפְּכוּ־\rb* \rb against me|בִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb My skin|בְּעוֹרִ֣י\rb* \rb and flesh|וּ֭בִבְשָׂרִי\rb* \rb cling|דָּבְקָ֣ה\rb* \rb to my bones|עַצְמִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I have escaped|וָ֝אֶתְמַלְּטָ֗ה\rb* \rb by the skin|בְּע֣וֹר\rb* \rb of my teeth|שִׁנָּֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Have pity on me|חָנֻּ֬נִי\rb*, \rb my friends|רֵעָ֑י\rb*, \rb have pity|חָנֻּ֣נִי\rb*\rb |אַתֶּ֣ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of God|אֱ֝ל֗וֹהַּ\rb* \rb has struck|נָ֣גְעָה\rb* \rb me|בִּֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb Why|לָ֭מָּה\rb* \rb do you persecute me|תִּרְדְּפֻ֣נִי\rb* \rb as|כְמוֹ־\rb* \rb God does|אֵ֑ל\rb*?
\q2 \rb Will you never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb get enough|תִשְׂבָּֽעוּ׃\rb* \rb of my flesh|וּ֝מִבְּשָׂרִ֗י\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 23 \rb I wish|מִֽי־\rb*\rb |יִתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֵ֭פוֹ\rb* \rb that my words|מִלָּ֑י\rb*\rb |מִֽי־\rb*\rb |יִתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb were recorded|וְיִכָּתְב֣וּן\rb*
\q2 \rb and inscribed|וְיֻחָֽקוּ׃\rb* \rb in a book|בַּסֵּ֣פֶר\rb*,
\q1 \v 24 \rb by an iron|בַּרְזֶ֥ל\rb* \rb stylus|בְּעֵט־\rb* \rb on lead|וְעֹפָ֑רֶת\rb*,
\q2 \rb or chiseled|יֵחָצְבֽוּן׃\rb* \rb in stone|בַּצּ֥וּר\rb* \rb forever|לָ֝עַ֗ד\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb But I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb know|יָ֭דַעְתִּי\rb* \rb that my Redeemer|גֹּ֣אֲלִי\rb*\f + \fr 19:25 \ft Or \fqa Vindicator\f* \rb lives|חָ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and in the end|וְ֝אַחֲר֗וֹן\rb* \rb He will stand|יָקֽוּם׃\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|עָפָ֥ר\rb*.\f + \fr 19:25 \ft Or \fqa on my grave\f*
\q1 \v 26 \rb Even after|וְאַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb my skin|ע֭וֹרִֽי\rb* \rb has been destroyed|נִקְּפוּ־\rb*,
\q2 \rb |זֹ֑את\rb* \rb yet in my flesh|וּ֝מִבְּשָׂרִ֗י\rb*\f + \fr 19:26 \ft Or \fqa without my flesh\f* \rb I will see|אֶֽחֱזֶ֥ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֽוֹהַּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb I|אֲנִ֨י׀\rb* \rb will see|אֶֽחֱזֶה־\rb* \rb Him|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb for myself|לִּ֗י\rb*;
\q2 \rb my eyes|וְעֵינַ֣י\rb* \rb will behold Him|רָא֣וּ\rb*, \rb and not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb as a stranger|זָ֑ר\rb*.
\q2 \rb How my heart|כִלְיֹתַ֣י\rb* \rb yearns|כָּל֖וּ\rb*\f + \fr 19:27 \ft Hebrew \fqa my kidneys yearn\f* \rb within me|בְּחֵקִֽי׃\rb*!
\b 
\q1 \v 28 \rb If|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you say|תֹ֭אמְרוּ\rb*, ‘\rb Let us|מַה־\rb* \rb persecute|נִּרְדָּף־\rb* \rb him|ל֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb since the root|וְשֹׁ֥רֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the matter|דָּ֝בָ֗ר\rb* \rb lies|נִמְצָא־\rb* \rb with him|בִֽי׃\rb*,\f + \fr 19:28 \ft Many Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Vulgate; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa with me\f*’
\q1 \v 29 \rb then you should fear|גּ֤וּרוּ\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵי־\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֗רֶב\rb* \rb yourselves|לָכֶ֨ם׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb wrath|חֵ֭מָה\rb* \rb brings punishment|עֲוֺנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb by the sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb you may know|תֵּדְע֣וּן\rb* \rb there is a judgment|שַׁדִּין׃ס\rb*.”
\c 20
\s1 Zophar: Destruction Awaits the Wicked
\p \v 1 \rb Then Zophar|צֹפַ֥ר\rb* \rb the Naamathite|הַנַּֽעֲמָתִ֗י\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb* \rb replied|וַ֭יַּעַן\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb So|לָ֭כֵן\rb* \rb my anxious thoughts|שְׂעִפַּ֣י\rb* \rb compel me to answer|יְשִׁיב֑וּנִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb because|וּ֝בַעֲב֗וּר\rb* \rb of the turmoil|ח֣וּשִׁי\rb* \rb within me|בִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb I have heard|אֶשְׁמָ֑ע\rb*\rb |וְ֝ר֗וּחַ\rb* \rb a rebuke|מוּסַ֣ר\rb* \rb that insults me|כְּלִמָּתִ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my understanding|מִֽבִּינָתִ֥י\rb* \rb prompts a reply|יַעֲנֵֽנִי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Do you not know|יָ֭דַעְתָּ\rb* \rb that|הֲזֹ֣את\rb* \rb from|מִנִּי־\rb* \rb antiquity|עַ֑ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb since|מִנִּ֤י\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb was placed|שִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵי־\rb* \rb the earth|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 5 \rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the triumph|רִנְנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְ֭שָׁעִים\rb* \rb has been brief|מִקָּר֑וֹב\rb*
\q2 \rb and the joy|וְשִׂמְחַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the godless|חָנֵ֣ף\rb*\rb |עֲדֵי־\rb* \rb momentary|רָֽגַע׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 6 \rb Though|אִם־\rb* \rb his arrogance|שִׂיא֑וֹ\rb* \rb reaches|יַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the heavens|לַשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and his head|וְ֝רֹאשׁ֗וֹ\rb* \rb touches|יַגִּֽיעַ׃\rb* \rb the clouds|לָעָ֥ב\rb*,
\q1 \v 7 \rb he will perish|יֹאבֵ֑ד\rb* \rb forever|לָנֶ֣צַח\rb*, \rb like his own dung|כְּֽ֭גֶלֲלוֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb those who had seen him|רֹ֝אָ֗יו\rb* \rb will ask|יֹאמְר֥וּ\rb*, ‘\rb Where is he|אַיּֽוֹ׃\rb*?’
\q1 \v 8 \rb He will fly away|יָ֭עוּף\rb* \rb like a dream|כַּחֲל֣וֹם\rb*, \rb never|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to be found|יִמְצָא֑וּהוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb he will be chased away|וְ֝יֻדַּ֗ד\rb* \rb like a vision|כְּחֶזְי֥וֹן\rb* \rb in the night|לָֽיְלָה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb The eye|עַ֣יִן\rb* \rb that saw him|שְׁ֭זָפַתּוּ\rb* \rb will see him no|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb more|תוֹסִ֑יף\rb*,
\q2 \rb and his place|מְקוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֝֗וֹד\rb* \rb behold him|תְּשׁוּרֶ֥נּוּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb His sons|בָּ֭נָיו\rb* \rb will seek the favor|יְרַצּ֣וּ\rb* \rb of the poor|דַלִּ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb for his own hands|וְ֝יָדָ֗יו\rb* \rb must return|תָּשֵׁ֥בְנָה\rb* \rb his wealth|אוֹנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb The youthful vigor|עֲלוּמוֹ\rb* \rb that fills|מָלְא֣וּ\rb* \rb his bones|עַ֭צְמוֹתָיו\rb*
\q2 \rb will lie down|תִּשְׁכָּֽב׃\rb* \rb with him|וְ֝עִמּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the dust|עָפָ֥ר\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb Though|אִם־\rb* \rb evil|רָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb is sweet|תַּמְתִּ֣יק\rb* \rb in his mouth|בְּפִ֣יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and he conceals|יַ֝כְחִידֶ֗נָּה\rb* \rb it under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb his tongue|לְשׁוֹנֽוֹ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 13 \rb though he cannot bear|יַחְמֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |עָ֭לֶיהָ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to let it go|יַֽעַזְבֶ֑נָּה\rb*
\q2 \rb and keeps|וְ֝יִמְנָעֶ֗נָּה\rb* \rb it in|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb his mouth|חִכּֽוֹ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 14 \rb yet in his stomach|בְּמֵעָ֣יו\rb* \rb his food|לַ֭חְמוֹ\rb* \rb sours|נֶהְפָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb into the venom|מְרוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of cobras|פְּתָנִ֣ים\rb* \rb within him|בְּקִרְבּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb He swallows|בָּ֭לַע\rb* \rb wealth|חַ֣יִל\rb* \rb but vomits it out|וַיְקִאֶ֑נּוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb God|אֵֽל׃\rb* \rb will force it|יוֹרִשֶׁ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb from his stomach|מִ֝בִּטְנ֗וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb He will suck|יִינָ֑ק\rb* \rb the poison|רֹאשׁ־\rb* \rb of cobras|פְּתָנִ֥ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb the fangs|לְשׁ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of a viper|אֶפְעֶֽה׃\rb* \rb will kill him|תַּֽ֝הַרְגֵ֗הוּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb He will not|אַל־\rb* \rb enjoy|יֵ֥רֶא\rb* \rb the streams|בִפְלַגּ֑וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb the rivers|נַהֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb flowing with|נַ֝חֲלֵ֗י\rb* \rb honey|דְּבַ֣שׁ\rb* \rb and cream|וְחֶמְאָֽה׃\rb*.
