\q2 \rb then, after|וְאַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb I have spoken|דַּבְּרִ֣י\rb*, \rb you may go on mocking|תַלְעִֽיג׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Is my|הֶ֭אָנֹכִי\rb* \rb complaint|שִׂיחִ֑י\rb*\rb |וְאִם־\rb* \rb against a man|לְאָדָ֣ם\rb*?
\q2 \rb Then why|מַ֝דּ֗וּעַ\rb* \rb should I not|לֹא־\rb*\rb |רוּחִֽי׃\rb* \rb be impatient|תִקְצַ֥ר\rb*?
\q1 \v 5 \rb Look|פְּנוּ־\rb* \rb at me|אֵלַ֥י\rb* \rb and be appalled|וְהָשַׁ֑מּוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb put|וְשִׂ֖ימוּ\rb* \rb your hand|יָ֣ד\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb your mouth|פֶּֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb When|וְאִם־\rb* \rb I remember|זָכַ֥רְתִּי\rb*, \rb terror|וְנִבְהָ֑לְתִּי\rb* \rb takes hold|וְאָחַ֥ז\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my body|בְּ֝שָׂרִ֗י\rb* \rb trembles in horror|פַּלָּצֽוּת׃\rb*.
