\q2 \rb completely|כֻּ֝לּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb secure|שַׁלְאֲנַ֥ן\rb* \rb and at ease|וְשָׁלֵֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb His body|עֲ֭טִינָיו\rb* \rb is well nourished|מָלְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |חָלָ֑ב\rb*,\f + \fr 21:24 \ft Literally \fqa His pails are full of milk\f*
\q2 \rb and his bones|עַצְמוֹתָ֣יו\rb* \rb are rich|יְשֻׁקֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb with marrow|וּמֹ֖חַ\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb Yet another man|וְזֶ֗ה\rb* \rb dies|יָ֭מוּת\rb* \rb in the bitterness|מָרָ֑ה\rb* \rb of his soul|בְּנֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb having never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb tasted|אָ֝כַ֗ל\rb* \rb prosperity|בַּטּוֹבָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb But together|יַ֭חַד\rb* \rb they lie down|יִשְׁכָּ֑בוּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the dust|עָפָ֣ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and worms|וְ֝רִמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb cover them|תְּכַסֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb both|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 27 \rb Behold|הֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb I know|יָ֭דַעְתִּי\rb* \rb your thoughts full well|מַחְשְׁבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb the schemes by which|וּ֝מְזִמּ֗וֹת\rb* \rb you would wrong|תַּחְמֹֽסוּ׃\rb* \rb me|עָלַ֥י\rb*.
\q1 \v 28 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you say|תֹֽאמְר֗וּ\rb*, ‘\rb Where|אַיֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb now is the nobleman’s|נָדִ֑יב\rb* \rb house|בֵית־\rb*,
\q2 \rb and where|וְ֝אַיֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb are the tents|אֹ֤הֶל׀\rb* \rb in which the wicked|רְשָׁעִֽים׃\rb* \rb dwell|מִשְׁכְּנ֬וֹת\rb*?’
\q1 \v 29 \rb Have you never|הֲלֹ֣א\rb* \rb asked|שְׁ֭אֶלְתֶּם\rb* \rb those who travel|ע֣וֹבְרֵי\rb* \rb the roads|דָ֑רֶךְ\rb*?
\q2 \rb Do you not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb accept|תְנַכֵּֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb their reports|וְ֝אֹתֹתָ֗ם\rb*?
\q1 \v 30 \rb Indeed|כִּ֤י\rb*, \rb the evil|רָ֑ע\rb* \rb man is spared|יֵחָ֣שֶׂךְ\rb* \rb from the day|לְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of calamity|אֵ֭יד\rb*,
\q2 \rb delivered|יוּבָֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb from the day|לְי֖וֹם\rb* \rb of wrath|עֲבָר֣וֹת\rb*.
\q1 \v 31 \rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb denounces|יַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb his behavior|דַּרְכּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֣יו\rb*?
\q2 \rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb repays|יְשַׁלֶּם־\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb for what he|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb has done|עָ֝שָׂ֗ה\rb*?
\q1 \v 32 \rb He|וְ֭הוּא\rb* \rb is carried|יוּבָ֑ל\rb* \rb to the grave|לִקְבָר֣וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and watch is kept|יִשְׁקֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb over|וְֽעַל־\rb* \rb his tomb|גָּדִ֥ישׁ\rb*.
\q1 \v 33 \rb The clods|רִגְבֵ֫י\rb* \rb of the valley|נָ֥חַל\rb* \rb are sweet|מָֽתְקוּ־\rb* \rb to him|ל֗וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb follows|יִמְשׁ֑וֹךְ\rb* \rb behind him|וְ֭אַחֲרָיו\rb*,
\q2 \rb and those before him|וּ֝לְפָנָ֗יו\rb* \rb are without|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb number|מִסְפָּֽר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 34 \rb So how|וְ֭אֵיךְ\rb* \rb can you comfort me|תְּנַחֲמ֣וּנִי\rb* \rb with empty words|הָ֑בֶל\rb*?
\q2 \rb For your answers|וּ֝תְשֽׁוּבֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb remain|נִשְׁאַר־\rb* \rb full of falsehood|מָֽעַל׃ס\rb*.”
\c 22
\s1 Eliphaz: Can a Man Be of Use to God?
\p \v 1 \rb Then Eliphaz|אֱלִיפַ֥ז\rb* \rb the Temanite|הַֽתֵּמָנִ֗י\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb* \rb replied|וַ֭יַּעַן\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb Can a man|גָּ֑בֶר\rb* \rb be of use|יִסְכָּן־\rb* \rb to God|הַלְאֵ֥ל\rb*?
\q2 \rb Can even|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a wise man|מַשְׂכִּֽיל׃\rb* \rb benefit|יִסְכֹּ֖ן\rb* \rb Him|עָלֵ֣ימוֹ\rb*?
\q1 \v 3 \rb Does it delight|הַחֵ֣פֶץ\rb* \rb the Almighty|לְ֭שַׁדַּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you are righteous|תִצְדָּ֑ק\rb*?
\q2 \rb |וְאִם־\rb* \rb Does He profit|בֶּ֝֗צַע\rb* \rb if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your ways|דְּרָכֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb are blameless|תַתֵּ֥ם\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Is it for your reverence|הֲֽ֭מִיִּרְאָ֣תְךָ\rb* \rb that He rebukes you|יֹכִיחֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and enters|יָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb into judgment|בַּמִּשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb* \rb against you|עִ֝מְּךָ֗\rb*?
\q1 \v 5 \rb Is not|הֲלֹ֣א\rb* \rb your wickedness|רָעָֽתְךָ֣\rb* \rb great|רַבָּ֑ה\rb*?
\q2 \rb Are not your iniquities|לַעֲוֺנֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb endless|וְאֵֽין־\rb*\rb |קֵ֝֗ץ\rb*?
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you needlessly|חִנָּ֑ם\rb* \rb demanded security|תַחְבֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb from your brothers|אַחֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and deprived|תַּפְשִֽׁיט׃\rb* \rb the naked|עֲרוּמִּ֣ים\rb* \rb of their clothing|וּבִגְדֵ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb You gave|תַּשְׁקֶ֑ה\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb water|מַ֭יִם\rb* \rb to the weary|עָיֵ֣ף\rb*
\q2 \rb and withheld|תִּֽמְנַֽע־\rb* \rb food|לָֽחֶם׃\rb* \rb from the famished|וּ֝מֵרָעֵ֗ב\rb*,
\q1 \v 8 \rb while the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb belonged to a mighty|זְ֭רוֹעַ\rb* \rb man|וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and a man|וּנְשׂ֥וּא\rb* \rb of honor|פָ֝נִ֗ים\rb* \rb lived|יֵ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb on it|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb You sent widows|אַ֭לְמָנוֹת\rb* \rb away|שִׁלַּ֣חְתָּ\rb* \rb empty-handed|רֵיקָ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the strength|וּזְרֹע֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the fatherless|יְתֹמִ֣ים\rb* \rb was crushed|יְדֻכָּֽא׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֭ן\rb* \rb snares|פַחִ֑ים\rb* \rb surround you|סְבִיבוֹתֶ֣יךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and sudden|פִּתְאֹֽם׃\rb* \rb peril|פַּ֣חַד\rb* \rb terrifies you|וִֽ֝יבַהֶלְךָ\rb*;
\q1 \v 11 \rb |אוֹ־\rb* \rb it is so dark|חֹ֥שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb you cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb see|תִרְאֶ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and a flood|וְֽשִׁפְעַת־\rb* \rb of water|מַ֥יִם\rb* \rb covers you|תְּכַסֶּֽךָּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb Is not|הֲ‍ֽלֹא־\rb* \rb God|אֱ֭לוֹהַּ\rb* \rb as high|גֹּ֣בַהּ\rb* \rb as the heavens|שָׁמָ֑יִם\rb*?
\q2 \rb Look at|וּרְאֵ֤ה\rb* \rb the highest|רֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb stars|כּוֹכָבִ֣ים\rb*, \rb how|כִּי־\rb* \rb lofty they are|רָֽמּוּ׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 13 \rb Yet you say|וְֽ֭אָמַרְתָּ\rb*: ‘\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb does God|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb know|יָּ֣דַֽע\rb*?
\q2 \rb Does He judge|יִשְׁפּֽוֹט׃\rb* \rb through|הַבְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb thick darkness|עֲרָפֶ֣ל\rb*?
\q1 \v 14 \rb Thick clouds|עָבִ֣ים\rb* \rb veil|סֵֽתֶר־\rb* \rb Him|ל֭וֹ\rb* \rb so He does not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb see us|יִרְאֶ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb as He traverses|יִתְהַלָּֽךְ׃\rb* \rb the vault|וְח֥וּג\rb* \rb of heaven|שָׁ֝מַ֗יִם\rb*.\f + \fr 22:14 \ft Or \fqa heaven’s horizon \ft or \fqa the circle of the sky\f*’
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb Will you stay|תִּשְׁמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb on the ancient|עוֹלָ֣ם\rb* \rb path|הַאֹ֣רַח\rb*
\q2 \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb wicked|אָֽוֶן׃\rb* \rb men|מְתֵי־\rb* \rb have trod|דָּרְכ֣וּ\rb*?
\q1 \v 16 \rb They|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb were snatched away|קֻמְּט֥וּ\rb* \rb before|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb their time|עֵ֑ת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and their foundations|יְסוֹדָֽם׃\rb* \rb were swept away|יוּצַ֥ק\rb* \rb by a flood|נָ֝הָ֗ר\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb They said|הָאֹמְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to God|לָ֭אֵל\rb*, ‘\rb Depart|ס֣וּר\rb* \rb from us|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*.
\q2 \rb What|וּמַה־\rb* \rb can the Almighty|שַׁדַּ֣י\rb* \rb do|יִּפְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb to us|לָֽמוֹ׃\rb*?’
\q1 \v 18 \rb But it was He|וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb who filled|מִלֵּ֣א\rb* \rb their houses|בָתֵּיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb with good things|ט֑וֹב\rb*;
\q2 \rb so I stay far|רָ֣חֲקָה\rb*\rb |מֶֽנִּי׃\rb* \rb from the counsel|וַעֲצַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְ֝שָׁעִ֗ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb The righteous|צַדִּיקִ֣ים\rb* \rb see it|יִרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb and are glad|וְיִשְׂמָ֑חוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb the innocent|וְ֝נָקִ֗י\rb* \rb mock|יִלְעַג־\rb* \rb them|לָֽמוֹ׃\rb*:
\q1 \v 20 ‘\rb Surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb our foes|קִימָ֑נוּ\rb* \rb are destroyed|נִכְחַ֣ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb and fire|אֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb has consumed|אָ֣כְלָה\rb* \rb their excess|וְ֝יִתְרָ֗ם\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Reconcile|הַסְכֶּן־\rb* \rb now|נָ֣א\rb* \rb and be at peace|וּשְׁלם\rb* \rb with Him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb thereby|בָּ֝הֶ֗ם\rb* \rb good|טוֹבָֽה׃\rb* \rb will come to you|תְּֽבוֹאַתְךָ֥\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb Receive|קַח־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb instruction|תּוֹרָ֑ה\rb* \rb from His mouth|מִפִּ֣יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb and lay up|וְשִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb His words|אֲ֝מָרָ֗יו\rb* \rb in your heart|בִּלְבָבֶֽךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you return|תָּשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Almighty|שַׁ֭דַּי\rb*, \rb you will be restored|תִּבָּנֶ֑ה\rb*.
\q2 \rb If you remove|תַּרְחִ֥יק\rb* \rb injustice|עַ֝וְלָ֗ה\rb* \rb from your tents|מֵאָהֳלֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 24 \rb and consign|וְשִׁית־\rb* \rb your gold|בָּ֑צֶר\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the dust|עָפָ֥ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and the gold of Ophir|אוֹפִֽיר׃\rb* \rb to the stones|וּבְצ֖וּר\rb* \rb of the ravines|נְחָלִ֣ים\rb*,
\q1 \v 25 \rb then the Almighty|שַׁדַּ֣י\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb your gold|בְּצָרֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the finest|תּוֹעָפ֣וֹת\rb* \rb silver|וְכֶ֖סֶף\rb* \rb for you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb Surely|כִּי־\rb* \rb then|אָ֭ז\rb* \rb you will delight|תִּתְעַנָּ֑ג\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Almighty|שַׁדַּ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb and lift up|וְתִשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|אֱל֣וֹהַּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb You will pray|תַּעְתִּ֣יר\rb* \rb to Him|אֵ֭לָיו\rb*, \rb and He will hear you|וְיִשְׁמָעֶ֑ךָּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and you will fulfill|תְשַׁלֵּֽם׃\rb* \rb your vows|וּנְדָרֶ֥יךָ\rb*.
\q1 \v 28 \rb Your decisions|וְֽתִגְזַר־\rb*\rb |א֭וֹמֶר\rb* \rb will be carried out|וְיָ֣קָם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and light|אֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb will shine|נָ֣גַֽהּ\rb* \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb your ways|דְּ֝רָכֶ֗יךָ\rb*.
\q1 \v 29 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb men are brought low|הִ֭שְׁפִּילוּ\rb* \rb and you say|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb Lift them up|גֵּוָ֑ה\rb*!’
\q2 \rb then He will save|יוֹשִֽׁעַ׃\rb* \rb the lowly|וְשַׁ֖ח\rb*\rb |עֵינַ֣יִם\rb*.
\q1 \v 30 \rb He will deliver even|יְֽמַלֵּ֥ט\rb* \rb one who is not|אִֽי־\rb* \rb innocent|נָקִ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb rescuing him|וְ֝נִמְלַ֗ט\rb* \rb through the cleanness|בְּבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb of your hands|כַּפֶּֽיךָ׃פ\rb*.”
\c 23
\s1 Job Longs for God
\p \v 1 \rb Then Job|אִיּ֗וֹב\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb Even|גַּם־\rb* \rb today|הַ֭יּוֹם\rb* \rb my complaint|שִׂחִ֑י\rb* \rb is bitter|מְרִ֣י\rb*.
\q2 \rb His hand|יָ֝דִ֗י\rb* \rb is heavy|כָּבְדָ֥ה\rb* \rb despite|עַל־\rb* \rb my groaning|אַנְחָתִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb If only|מִֽי־\rb*\rb |יִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb I knew|יָ֭דַעְתִּי\rb* \rb where to find Him|וְאֶמְצָאֵ֑הוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that I could go|אָ֝ב֗וֹא\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb His seat|תְּכוּנָתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb I would plead|אֶעֶרְכָ֣ה\rb* \rb my case|מִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb* \rb before Him|לְפָנָ֣יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and fill my mouth|וּ֝פִ֗י\rb* \rb with|אֲמַלֵּ֥א\rb* \rb arguments|תוֹכָחֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb I would learn|אֵ֭דְעָה\rb* \rb how|מִלִּ֣ים\rb* \rb He would answer|יַעֲנֵ֑נִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and consider|וְ֝אָבִ֗ינָה\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb He would say|יֹּ֥אמַר\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Would He contend|יָרִ֣יב\rb* \rb with me|עִמָּדִ֑י\rb* \rb in His great|הַבְּרָב־\rb* \rb power|כֹּ֭חַ\rb*?
\q2 \rb No|לֹ֥א\rb*, \rb He|ה֝֗וּא\rb* \rb would certainly|אַךְ־\rb* \rb take note|יָשִׂ֥ם\rb* \rb of me|בִּֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb Then|שָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb an upright man|יָ֭שָׁר\rb* \rb could reason|נוֹכָ֣ח\rb* \rb with Him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I would be delivered|וַאֲפַלְּטָ֥ה\rb* \rb forever|לָ֝נֶ֗צַח\rb* \rb from my Judge|מִשֹּׁפְטִֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb If|הֵ֤ן\rb* \rb I go|אֶהֱלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb east|קֶ֣דֶם\rb*, \rb He is not there|וְאֵינֶ֑נּוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and if I go west|וְ֝אָח֗וֹר\rb*, \rb I cannot|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb find|אָבִ֥ין\rb* \rb Him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb When He is at work|בַּעֲשֹׂת֣וֹ\rb* \rb in the north|שְׂמֹ֣אול\rb*, \rb I cannot|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb behold Him|אָ֑חַז\rb*;
\q2 \rb when He turns|יַעְטֹ֥ף\rb* \rb to the south|יָ֝מִ֗ין\rb*, \rb I cannot|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb see Him|אֶרְאֶֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Yet|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He knows|יָ֭דַע\rb* \rb the way I have taken|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb*\rb |עִמָּדִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb when He has tested me|בְּ֝חָנַ֗נִי\rb*, \rb I will come forth|אֵצֵֽא׃\rb* \rb as gold|כַּזָּהָ֥ב\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb My feet|רַגְלִ֑י\rb* \rb have followed|אָחֲזָ֣ה\rb* \rb in His tracks|בַּ֭אֲשֻׁרוֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb I have kept|שָׁמַ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb His way|דַּרְכּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb without|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb turning aside|אָֽט׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb I have not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb departed|אָמִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb from the command|מִצְוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of His lips|שְׂ֭פָתָיו\rb*;
\q2 \rb I have treasured|צָפַ֥נְתִּי\rb* \rb the words|אִמְרֵי־\rb* \rb of His mouth|פִֽיו׃\rb*
\q2 \rb more than my daily bread|מֵ֝חֻקִּ֗י\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb But He is unchangeable|וְה֣וּא\rb*\rb |בְ֭אֶחָד\rb*, \rb and who|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb can oppose Him|יְשִׁיבֶ֑נּוּ\rb*?
\q2 \rb He does|וַיָּֽעַשׂ׃\rb* \rb what He|וְנַפְשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb desires|אִוְּתָ֣ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb For|כִּ֭י\rb* \rb He carries out|יַשְׁלִ֣ים\rb* \rb His decree against me|חֻקִּ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and He has|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb many|רַבּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb such plans|וְכָהֵ֖נָּה\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֭ן\rb* \rb I am terrified|אֶבָּהֵ֑ל\rb* \rb in His presence|מִפָּנָ֣יו\rb*;
\q2 \rb when I consider this|אֶ֝תְבּוֹנֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb I fear|וְאֶפְחַ֥ד\rb* \rb Him|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb God|וְ֭אֵל\rb* \rb has made my heart|לִבִּ֑י\rb* \rb faint|הֵרַ֣ךְ\rb*;
\q2 \rb the Almighty|וְ֝שַׁדַּ֗י\rb* \rb has terrified me|הִבְהִילָֽנִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb Yet|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I am not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb silenced|נִ֭צְמַתִּי\rb* \rb by|מִפְּנֵי־\rb* \rb the darkness|חֹ֑שֶׁךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb by the thick darkness|אֹֽפֶל׃\rb* \rb that covers|כִּסָּה־\rb* \rb my face|וּ֝מִפָּנַ֗י\rb*.[’’]
\c 24
\s1 Job: Judgment for the Wicked
\q1 \v 1 “\rb Why|מַדּ֗וּעַ\rb* \rb does the Almighty|מִ֭שַּׁדַּי\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb reserve|נִצְפְּנ֣וּ\rb* \rb times for judgment|עִתִּ֑ים\rb*?
\q2 \rb Why may those who know Him|וְיֹדְעוֹ\rb* \rb never|לֹא־\rb* \rb see|חָ֥זוּ\rb* \rb His days|יָמָֽיו׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 2 \rb Men move|יַשִּׂ֑יגוּ\rb* \rb boundary stones|גְּבֻל֥וֹת\rb*;
\q2 \rb they pasture|וַיִּרְעֽוּ׃\rb* \rb stolen|גָּ֝זְל֗וּ\rb* \rb flocks|עֵ֥דֶר\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb They drive away|יִנְהָ֑גוּ\rb* \rb the donkey|חֲמ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of the fatherless|יְתוֹמִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and take the widow’s|אַלְמָנָֽה׃\rb* \rb ox|שׁ֣וֹר\rb* \rb in pledge|יַ֝חְבְּל֗וּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb They push|יַטּ֣וּ\rb* \rb the needy|אֶבְיוֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb off the road|מִדָּ֑רֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and force all|יַ֥חַד\rb* \rb the poor|עֲנִיֵּי־\rb* \rb of the land|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb into hiding|חֻ֝בְּא֗וּ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb Indeed|הֵ֤ן\rb*, \rb like wild donkeys|פְּרָאִ֨ים׀\rb* \rb in the desert|בַּֽמִּדְבָּ֗ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb the poor go|יָצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb to work|בְּ֭פָעֳלָם\rb* \rb foraging|מְשַׁחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb for food|לַטָּ֑רֶף\rb*;
\q2 \rb the wasteland|עֲרָבָ֥ה\rb* \rb is food|לֶ֝֗חֶם\rb* \rb for their children|לַנְּעָרִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb They gather|יַקְצִירוּ\rb* \rb fodder|בְּלִיל֣וֹ\rb* \rb in the fields|בַּ֭שָּׂדֶה\rb*
\q2 \rb and glean|יְלַקֵּֽשׁוּ׃\rb* \rb the vineyards|וְכֶ֖רֶם\rb* \rb of the wicked|רָשָׁ֣ע\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb Without|מִבְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb clothing|לְב֑וּשׁ\rb*, \rb they spend the night|יָ֭לִינוּ\rb* \rb naked|עָר֣וֹם\rb*;
\q2 \rb they have no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb covering|כְּ֝ס֗וּת\rb* \rb against the cold|בַּקָּרָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb Drenched|יִרְטָ֑בוּ\rb* \rb by mountain|הָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb rains|מִזֶּ֣רֶם\rb*,
\q2 \rb they huddle|חִבְּקוּ־\rb* \rb against the rocks|צֽוּר׃\rb* \rb for want|וּֽמִבְּלִ֥י\rb* \rb of shelter|מַ֝חְסֶ֗ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb The fatherless infant|יָת֑וֹם\rb* \rb is snatched|יִ֭גְזְלוּ\rb* \rb from the breast|מִשֹּׁ֣ד\rb*;
\q2 \rb the nursing child|וְֽעַל־\rb* \rb of the poor|עָנִ֥י\rb* \rb is seized for a debt|יַחְבֹּֽלוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Without|בְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb clothing|לְב֑וּשׁ\rb*, \rb they wander about|הִ֭לְּכוּ\rb* \rb naked|עָר֣וֹם\rb*.
\q2 \rb They carry|נָ֣שְׂאוּ\rb* \rb the sheaves|עֹֽמֶר׃\rb*, \rb but still go hungry|וּ֝רְעֵבִ֗ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb They crush olives|יַצְהִ֑ירוּ\rb* \rb within|בֵּין־\rb* \rb their walls|שׁוּרֹתָ֥ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb they tread|דָּ֝רְכ֗וּ\rb* \rb the winepresses|יְקָבִ֥ים\rb*, \rb but go thirsty|וַיִּצְמָֽאוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb From the city|מֵ֘עִ֤יר\rb*, \rb men|מְתִ֨ים׀\rb* \rb groan|יִנְאָ֗קוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the souls|וְנֶֽפֶשׁ־\rb* \rb of the wounded|חֲלָלִ֥ים\rb* \rb cry out|תְּשַׁוֵּ֑עַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb yet God|וֶ֝אֱל֗וֹהַּ\rb* \rb charges|יָשִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb no one|לֹא־\rb* \rb with wrongdoing|תִּפְלָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Then there|הֵ֤מָּה׀\rb* \rb are|הָיוּ֮\rb* \rb those who rebel|בְּֽמֹרְדֵ֫י־\rb* \rb against the light|א֥וֹר\rb*,
\q2 \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb knowing|הִכִּ֥ירוּ\rb* \rb its ways|דְרָכָ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or staying|יָ֝שְׁב֗וּ\rb* \rb on its paths|בִּנְתִיבֹתָֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb When daylight is gone|לָא֡וֹר\rb*, \rb the murderer|רוֹצֵ֗חַ\rb* \rb rises|יָ֘ק֤וּם\rb*
\q2 \rb to kill|יִֽקְטָל־\rb* \rb the poor|עָנִ֥י\rb* \rb and needy|וְאֶבְי֑וֹן\rb*;
\q2 \rb in the night|וּ֝בַלַּ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb he is|יְהִ֣י\rb* \rb like a thief|כַגַּנָּֽב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb The eye|וְעֵ֤ין\rb* \rb of the adulterer|נֹאֵ֨ף׀\rb* \rb watches|שָׁ֤מְרָֽה\rb* \rb for twilight|נֶ֣שֶׁף\rb*.
\q2 \rb Thinking|לֵ֭אמֹר\rb*, ‘\rb No|לֹא־\rb* \rb eye|עָ֑יִן\rb* \rb will see me|תְשׁוּרֵ֣נִי\rb*,’ \rb he covers|וְסֵ֖תֶר\rb*\rb |יָשִֽׂים׃\rb* \rb his face|פָּנִ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb In the dark|בַּחֹ֗שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb they dig through|חָתַ֥ר\rb* \rb houses|בָּ֫תִּ֥ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb by day|יוֹמָ֥ם\rb* \rb they shut themselves in|חִתְּמוּ־\rb*,
\q2 \rb never|לֹא־\rb* \rb to experience|יָ֥דְעוּ\rb* \rb the light|אֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb to them|לָ֣מוֹ\rb*, \rb deep darkness|צַלְמָ֑וֶת\rb* \rb is their|יַחְדָּ֨ו׀\rb* \rb morning|בֹּ֣קֶר\rb*;
\q2 \rb surely|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they are friends with|יַ֝כִּ֗יר\rb* \rb the terrors|בַּלְה֥וֹת\rb* \rb of darkness|צַלְמָֽוֶת׃\rb*!
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb They|ה֤וּא׀\rb* \rb are but foam|קַֽל־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the surface|פְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of the water|מַ֗יִם\rb*;
\q2 \rb their portion|חֶלְקָתָ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb is cursed|תְּקֻלַּ֣ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that no one|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb turns|יִ֝פְנֶה\rb* \rb toward|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb their vineyards|כְּרָמִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb As drought|צִיָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and|גַם־\rb* \rb heat|חֹ֗ם\rb* \rb consume|יִגְזְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |מֵֽימֵי־\rb* \rb the melting snow|שֶׁ֗לֶג\rb*,
\q2 \rb so Sheol|שְׁא֣וֹל\rb* \rb steals those who have sinned|חָטָֽאוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb The womb|רֶ֨חֶם׀\rb* \rb forgets them|יִשְׁכָּ֘חֵ֤הוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb the worm|רִמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb feeds on them|מְתָ֘ק֤וֹ\rb*;
\q1 \rb they are remembered|יִזָּכֵ֑ר\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb more|ע֥וֹד\rb*.
\q2 \rb So injustice|עַוְלָֽה׃\rb* \rb is broken|וַתִּשָּׁבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb like a tree|כָּעֵ֣ץ\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb They prey|רֹעֶ֣ה\rb* \rb on the barren|עֲ֭קָרָה\rb* \rb and childless|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |תֵלֵ֑ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb and show no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb kindness|יְיֵטִֽיב׃\rb* \rb to the widow|וְ֝אַלְמָנָ֗ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb Yet by His power|בְּכֹח֑וֹ\rb*, \rb God drags away|וּמָשַׁ֣ךְ\rb* \rb the mighty|אַבִּירִ֣ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb though rising up|יָ֝ק֗וּם\rb*, \rb they have no|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb assurance|יַאֲמִ֥ין\rb* \rb of life|בַּֽחַיִּֽין׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb He gives|יִתֶּן־\rb* \rb them|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb a sense of security|לָ֭בֶטַח\rb*\rb |וְיִשָּׁעֵ֑ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb but His eyes|וְ֝עֵינֵ֗יהוּ\rb* \rb are on|עַל־\rb* \rb their ways|דַּרְכֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb They are exalted|ר֤וֹמּוּ\rb* \rb for a moment|מְּעַ֨ט׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb then they are gone|וְֽאֵינֶ֗נּוּ\rb*;
\q1 \rb they are brought low|וְֽהֻמְּכ֗וּ\rb* \rb and gathered up|יִקָּפְצ֑וּן\rb* \rb like all others|כַּכֹּ֥ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb they are cut off|יִמָּֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb like heads|וּכְרֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb of grain|שִׁבֹּ֣לֶת\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb this is not so|לֹ֣א\rb*, \rb then|אֵ֭פוֹ\rb* \rb who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb can prove me a liar|יַכְזִיבֵ֑נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and reduce|וְיָשֵׂ֥ם\rb* \rb my words|מִלָּתִֽי׃ס\rb* \rb to nothing|לְ֝אַ֗ל\rb*?”
\c 25
\s1 Bildad: Man Cannot Be Righteous
\p \v 1 \rb Then Bildad|בִּלְדַּ֥ד\rb* \rb the Shuhite|הַשֻּׁחִ֗י\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb* \rb replied|וַ֭יַּעַן\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb Dominion|הַמְשֵׁ֣ל\rb* \rb and awe|וָפַ֣חַד\rb* \rb belong to God|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb He establishes|עֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb harmony|שָׁ֝ל֗וֹם\rb* \rb in the heights of heaven|בִּמְרוֹמָֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb |הֲיֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb Can His troops|לִגְדוּדָ֑יו\rb* \rb be numbered|מִ֭סְפָּר\rb*?
\q2 \rb On|וְעַל־\rb* \rb whom|מִ֝֗י\rb* \rb does His light|אוֹרֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb rise|יָק֥וּם\rb*?
\q1 \v 4 \rb How|וּמַה־\rb* \rb then can a man|אֱנ֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb be just|יִּצְדַּ֣ק\rb* \rb before|עִם־\rb* \rb God|אֵ֑ל\rb*?
\q2 \rb How|וּמַה־\rb* \rb can one born|יְל֣וּד\rb* \rb of woman|אִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \rb be pure|יִּ֝זְכֶּ֗ה\rb*?
\q1 \v 5 \rb If|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb even|עַד־\rb* \rb the moon|יָ֭רֵחַ\rb* \rb does not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb shine|יַאֲהִ֑יל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the stars|וְ֝כוֹכָבִ֗ים\rb* \rb are not|לֹא־\rb* \rb pure|זַכּ֥וּ\rb* \rb in His sight|בְעֵינָֽיו׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 6 \rb how much less|אַ֭ף\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb man|אֱנ֣וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb who is but a maggot|רִמָּ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the son|וּבֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָ֝דָ֗ם\rb*, \rb who is but a worm|תּוֹלֵעָֽה׃פ\rb*!”
\c 26
\s1 Job: Who Can Understand God’s Majesty?
\p \v 1 \rb Then Job|אִיּ֗וֹב\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb How|מֶה־\rb* \rb you have helped|עָזַ֥רְתָּ\rb* \rb the powerless|לְלֹא־\rb*\rb |כֹ֑חַ\rb*
\q2 \rb and saved|ה֝וֹשַׁ֗עְתָּ\rb* \rb the arm|זְר֣וֹעַ\rb* \rb that is feeble|לֹא־\rb*\rb |עֹֽז׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 3 \rb How|מַה־\rb* \rb you have counseled|יָּ֭עַצְתָּ\rb* \rb the unwise|לְלֹ֣א\rb*\rb |חָכְמָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and provided|הוֹדָֽעְתָּ׃\rb* \rb fully sound|לָרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb insight|וְ֝תוּשִׁיָּ֗ה\rb*!
\q1 \v 4 \rb To|אֶת־\rb* \rb whom|מִ֭י\rb* \rb have you uttered|הִגַּ֣דְתָּ\rb* \rb these words|מִלִּ֑ין\rb*?
\q2 \rb And whose|מִ֝י\rb* \rb spirit|וְנִשְׁמַת־\rb* \rb spoke|יָצְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb through you|מִמֶּֽךָּ׃\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb The dead|הָרְפָאִ֥ים\rb* \rb tremble|יְחוֹלָ֑לוּ\rb* —
\q2 \rb those beneath|מִתַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the waters|מַ֝֗יִם\rb* \rb and those who dwell in them|וְשֹׁכְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Sheol|שְׁא֣וֹל\rb* \rb is naked|עָר֣וֹם\rb* \rb before God|נֶגְדּ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and Abaddon|לָֽאֲבַדּֽוֹן׃\rb*\f + \fr 26:6 \fqa Abaddon \ft means \fqa Destruction\ft .\f* \rb has no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb covering|כְּ֝ס֗וּת\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb He stretches out|נֹטֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the north|צָפ֣וֹן\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb empty space|תֹּ֑הוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb He hangs|תֹּ֥לֶה\rb* \rb the earth|אֶ֝֗רֶץ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb nothing|בְּלִי־\rb*\rb |מָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb He wraps up|צֹרֵֽר־\rb* \rb the waters|מַ֥יִם\rb* \rb in His clouds|בְּעָבָ֑יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb yet the clouds|עָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb do not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb burst|נִבְקַ֖ע\rb* \rb under their own weight|תַּחְתָּֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb He covers|מְאַחֵ֥ז\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of the full moon|כִסֵּ֑ה\rb*,\f + \fr 26:9 \ft Or \fqa of His throne\f*
\q2 \rb spreading|פַּרְשֵׁ֖ז\rb* \rb over it|עָלָ֣יו\rb* \rb His cloud|עֲנָנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb He has inscribed|חָ֭ג\rb* \rb a horizon|חֹֽק־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of the waters|מָ֑יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb at|עַד־\rb* \rb the boundary|תַּכְלִ֖ית\rb* \rb between|עִם־\rb* \rb light|א֣וֹר\rb* \rb and darkness|חֹֽשֶׁךְ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb The foundations|עַמּוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of heaven|שָׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb quake|יְרוֹפָ֑פוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb astounded|וְ֝יִתְמְה֗וּ\rb* \rb at His rebuke|מִגַּעֲרָתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb By His power|בְּ֭כֹחוֹ\rb* \rb He stirred|רָגַ֣ע\rb*\f + \fr 26:12 \ft Or \fqa stilled\f* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֑ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb by His understanding|וּבִתוּבְנָתוֹ\rb* \rb He shattered|מָ֣חַץ\rb* \rb Rahab|רָֽהַב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb By His breath|בְּ֭רוּחוֹ\rb* \rb the skies|שָׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb were cleared|שִׁפְרָ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb His hand|יָ֝ד֗וֹ\rb* \rb pierced|חֹֽלֲלָ֥ה\rb* \rb the fleeing|בָּרִֽיחַ׃\rb* \rb serpent|נָחָ֥שׁ\rb*.\f + \fr 26:13 \ft Hebrew \fqa nachash\ft ; translated in most cases as \fqa snake\f*
\q1 \v 14 \rb Indeed|הֶן־\rb*, \rb these are|אֵ֤לֶּה׀\rb* \rb but the fringes|קְצ֬וֹת\rb* \rb of His ways|דַּרְכּוֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb how|וּמַה־\rb* \rb faint|שֵּׁ֣מֶץ\rb* \rb is the whisper|דָּ֭בָר\rb* \rb we hear|נִשְׁמַע־\rb* \rb of Him|בּ֑וֹ\rb*!
\q1 \rb Who then|מִ֣י\rb* \rb can understand|יִתְבּוֹנָֽן׃ס\rb*
\q2 \rb the thunder|וְרַ֥עַם\rb* \rb of His power|גְּבוּרָתוֹ\rb*?”
\c 27
\s1 Job Affirms His Integrity
\p \v 1 \rb Job|אִ֭יּוֹב\rb*\rb |שְׂאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb continued|וַיֹּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb his discourse|מְשָׁל֗וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb As surely as God|אֵ֭ל\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb who has deprived me of|הֵסִ֣יר\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּטִ֑י\rb* —
\q2 \rb the Almighty|וְ֝שַׁדַּ֗י\rb*, \rb who has embittered|הֵמַ֥ר\rb* \rb my soul|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb* —
