\c 29
\s1 Job’s Former Blessings
\p \v 1 \rb And Job|אִ֭יּוֹב\rb*\rb |שְׂאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb continued|וַיֹּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb his discourse|מְשָׁל֗וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb How I long|מִֽי־\rb*\rb |יִתְּנֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb for the months|כְיַרְחֵי־\rb* \rb gone by|קֶ֑דֶם\rb*,
\q2 \rb for the days|כִּ֝ימֵ֗י\rb* \rb when God|אֱל֣וֹהַּ\rb* \rb watched over me|יִשְׁמְרֵֽנִי׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 3 \rb when His lamp|נֵ֭רוֹ\rb* \rb shone|בְּהִלּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb above|עֲלֵ֣י\rb* \rb my head|רֹאשִׁ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and by His light|לְ֝אוֹרוֹ\rb* \rb I walked|אֵ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb through the darkness|חֹֽשֶׁךְ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 4 \rb when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I was|הָ֭יִיתִי\rb*\rb |בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb in my prime|חָרְפִּ֑י\rb*,\f + \fr 29:4 \ft Hebrew \fqa in the time of my harvest\f*
\q2 \rb when the friendship|בְּס֥וֹד\rb* \rb of God|אֱ֝ל֗וֹהַּ\rb* \rb rested on|עֲלֵ֣י\rb* \rb my tent|אָהֳלִֽי׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 5 \rb when the Almighty|שַׁ֭דַּי\rb* \rb was still|בְּע֣וֹד\rb* \rb with me|עִמָּדִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and my children|נְעָרָֽי׃\rb* \rb were around me|סְבִ֖יבוֹתַ֣י\rb*,
\q1 \v 6 \rb when my steps|הֲלִיכַ֣י\rb* \rb were bathed|בִּרְחֹ֣ץ\rb* \rb in cream|בְּחֵמָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and the rock|וְצ֥וּר\rb* \rb poured out|יָצ֥וּק\rb* \rb for me|עִ֝מָּדִ֗י\rb* \rb streams|פַּלְגֵי־\rb* \rb of oil|שָֽׁמֶן׃\rb*!
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb When I went out|בְּצֵ֣אתִי\rb* \rb to the city|קָ֑רֶת\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*\rb |עֲלֵי־\rb*
\q2 \rb and took|אָכִ֥ין\rb* \rb my seat|מוֹשָׁבִֽי׃\rb* \rb in the public square|בָּ֝רְח֗וֹב\rb*,
\q1 \v 8 \rb the young men|נְעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb saw me|רָא֣וּנִי\rb* \rb and withdrew|וְנֶחְבָּ֑אוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the old men|וִֽ֝ישִׁישִׁים\rb* \rb rose|קָ֣מוּ\rb* \rb to their feet|עָמָֽדוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb The princes|שָׂ֭רִים\rb* \rb refrained|עָצְר֣וּ\rb* \rb from speaking|בְמִלִּ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and covered|יָשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb their mouths|לְפִיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb with their hands|וְ֝כַ֗ף\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb The voices|קוֹל־\rb* \rb of the nobles|נְגִידִ֥ים\rb* \rb were hushed|נֶחְבָּ֑אוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and their tongues|וּ֝לְשׁוֹנָ֗ם\rb* \rb stuck|דָּבֵֽקָה׃\rb* \rb to the roofs of their mouths|לְחִכָּ֥ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb those|אֹ֣זֶן\rb* \rb who heard me|שָׁ֭מְעָה\rb* \rb called me blessed|וַֽתְּאַשְּׁרֵ֑נִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and those who|וְעַ֥יִן\rb* \rb saw me|רָ֝אֲתָ֗ה\rb* \rb commended me|וַתְּעִידֵֽנִי׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 12 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I rescued|אֲ֭מַלֵּט\rb* \rb the poor|עָנִ֣י\rb* \rb who cried out|מְשַׁוֵּ֑עַ\rb*
