\q1 \v 15 \rb I served as|הָ֭יִיתִי\rb* \rb eyes|עֵינַ֣יִם\rb* \rb to the blind|לַֽעִוֵּ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb as feet|וְרַגְלַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to the lame|לַפִּסֵּ֣חַ\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb I|אָ֭נֹכִֽי\rb* \rb was a father|אָ֣ב\rb* \rb to the needy|לָֽאֶבְיוֹנִ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I took up|אֶחְקְרֵֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb the case|וְרִ֖ב\rb* \rb of the stranger|לֹא־\rb*\rb |יָדַ֣עְתִּי\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb I shattered|וָֽ֭אֲשַׁבְּרָה\rb* \rb the fangs|מְתַלְּע֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the unjust|עַוָּ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and snatched|אַשְׁלִ֥יךְ\rb* \rb the prey|טָֽרֶף׃\rb* \rb from his teeth|וּ֝מִשִּׁנָּ֗יו\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb So I thought|וָ֭אֹמַר\rb*: ‘\rb I will die|אֶגְוָ֑ע\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb my nest|קִנִּ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb and multiply|אַרְבֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb my days|יָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb as the sand|וְ֝כַח֗וֹל\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb My roots|שָׁרְשִׁ֣י\rb* \rb will spread out|פָת֣וּחַ\rb* \rb to|אֱלֵי־\rb* \rb the waters|מָ֑יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the dew|וְ֝טַ֗ל\rb* \rb will rest nightly|יָלִ֥ין\rb* \rb on my branches|בִּקְצִירִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb My glory|כְּ֭בוֹדִי\rb* \rb is ever new|חָדָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb within me|עִמָּדִ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my bow|וְ֝קַשְׁתִּ֗י\rb* \rb is renewed|תַחֲלִֽיף׃\rb* \rb in my hand|בְּיָדִ֥י\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Men listened|שָׁמְע֥וּ\rb* \rb to me|לִֽי־\rb* \rb with expectation|וְיִחֵ֑לּוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb waiting silently|וְ֝יִדְּמ֗וּ\rb* \rb for|לְמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb my counsel|עֲצָתִֽי׃\rb*.
