\q2 \rb my speech|מִלָּתִֽי׃\rb* \rb settled|תִּטֹּ֥ף\rb* \rb on them like dew|וְ֝עָלֵ֗ימוֹ\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb They waited|וְיִֽחֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb for me as for rain|כַמָּטָ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and drank in my words|פָּעֲר֥וּ\rb*\rb |וּ֝פִיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb like spring showers|לְמַלְקֽוֹשׁ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb If I smiled|אֶשְׂחַ֣ק\rb* \rb at them|אֲ֭לֵהֶם\rb*, \rb they did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb believe it|יַאֲמִ֑ינוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb the light|וְא֥וֹר\rb* \rb of my countenance|פָּ֝נַ֗י\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb was precious|יַפִּילֽוּן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb I chose|אֶֽבֲחַ֣ר\rb* \rb their course|דַּרְכָּם֮\rb* \rb and presided|וְאֵשֵׁ֪ב\rb* \rb as chief|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb*.
\q2 \rb So I dwelt|וְ֭אֶשְׁכּוֹן\rb* \rb as a king|כְּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb among his troops|בַּגְּד֑וּד\rb*,
\q2 \rb as a comforter|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |יְנַחֵֽם׃\rb* \rb of the mourners|אֲבֵלִ֣ים\rb*.[’’]
\c 30
\s1 Job’s Honor Turned to Contempt
\q1 \v 1 “\rb But now|וְעַתָּ֤ה׀\rb* \rb they mock me|שָֽׂחֲק֣וּ\rb*\rb |עָלַי֮\rb*,
\q2 \rb men younger|צְעִירִ֥ים\rb* \rb than I am|מִמֶּ֗נִּי\rb*,\rb |לְיָ֫מִ֥ים\rb*
\q1 \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb I would have refused|מָאַ֥סְתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb to put|לָ֝שִׁ֗ית\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb my sheep|צֹאנִֽי׃\rb* \rb dogs|כַּלְבֵ֥י\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb What use|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb to me|לִּ֑י\rb*\rb |עָ֝לֵ֗ימוֹ\rb* \rb was the strength|כֹּ֣חַ\rb* \rb of their hands|יְ֭דֵיהֶם\rb*,
\q2 \rb since their vigor|כָּֽלַח׃\rb* \rb had left them|אָ֣בַד\rb*?
\q1 \v 3 \rb Gaunt|גַּ֫לְמ֥וּד\rb* \rb from poverty|בְּחֶ֥סֶר\rb* \rb and hunger|וּבְכָפָ֗ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb they gnawed|הַֽעֹרְקִ֥ים\rb* \rb the dry land|צִיָּ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the desolate|שׁוֹאָ֥ה\rb* \rb wasteland|וּמְשֹׁאָֽה׃\rb* \rb by night|אֶ֝֗מֶשׁ\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb They plucked|הַקֹּטְפִ֣ים\rb* \rb mallow|מַלּ֣וּחַ\rb* \rb among|עֲלֵי־\rb* \rb the shrubs|שִׂ֑יחַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the roots|וְשֹׁ֖רֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the broom tree|רְתָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb were their food|לַחְמָֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:4 \ft Or \fqa their fuel\f*
\q1 \v 5 \rb They were banished|יְגֹרָ֑שׁוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb among men|גֵּ֥ו\rb*,
\q2 \rb shouted|יָרִ֥יעוּ\rb* \rb at|עָ֝לֵ֗ימוֹ\rb* \rb like thieves|כַּגַּנָּֽב׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 6 \rb so that they lived|לִשְׁכֹּ֑ן\rb* \rb on the slopes|בַּעֲר֣וּץ\rb* \rb of the wadis|נְחָלִ֣ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb among the rocks|וְכֵפִֽים׃\rb* \rb and in holes|חֹרֵ֖י\rb* \rb in the ground|עָפָ֣ר\rb*.
