\q2 \rb and huddled|יְסֻפָּֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb beneath|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the nettles|חָר֣וּל\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb A senseless|נָ֭בָל\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb*\rb |בְלִי־\rb* \rb nameless|שֵׁ֑ם\rb* \rb brood|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb they were driven|נִ֝כְּא֗וּ\rb* \rb off|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb And now|וְ֭עַתָּה\rb*\rb |הָיִ֑יתִי\rb* \rb they mock me in song|נְגִינָתָ֣ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb I have become|וָאֱהִ֖י\rb* \rb a byword|לְמִלָּֽה׃\rb* \rb among them|לָהֶ֣ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb They abhor me|תִּֽ֭עֲבוּנִי\rb* \rb and keep far|רָ֣חֲקוּ\rb* \rb from me|מֶ֑נִּי\rb*;
\q2 \rb they do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb hesitate|חָ֥שְׂכוּ\rb* \rb to spit|רֹֽק׃\rb* \rb in my face|וּ֝מִפָּנַ֗י\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God has unstrung|פִ֭תַּח\rb* \rb my bow|יִתְרוֹ\rb* \rb and afflicted me|וַיְעַנֵּ֑נִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb they have cast off|שִׁלֵּֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb restraint|וְ֝רֶ֗סֶן\rb*\f + \fr 30:11 \ft Hebrew \fqa the bridle\f* \rb in my presence|מִפָּנַ֥י\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb The rabble|פִּרְחַ֪ח\rb* \rb arises|יָ֫ק֥וּמוּ\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb my right|יָמִין֮\rb*;
\q2 \rb they lay snares|שִׁלֵּ֑חוּ\rb* \rb for my feet|רַגְלַ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb and build|וַיָּסֹ֥לּוּ\rb* \rb siege ramps|אָרְח֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֵידָֽם׃\rb* \rb against me|עָ֝לַ֗י\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb They tear up|נָתְס֗וּ\rb* \rb my path|נְֽתִיבָ֫תִ֥י\rb*;
\q2 \rb they profit|יֹעִ֑ילוּ\rb* \rb from my destruction|לְהַוָּתִ֥י\rb*,
\q2 \rb with no one|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb to restrain|עֹזֵ֣ר\rb* \rb them|לָֽמוֹ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:13 \ft Or \fqa with no one to assist them\f*
\q1 \v 14 \rb They advance|יֶאֱתָ֑יוּ\rb* \rb as through a wide|רָחָ֣ב\rb* \rb breach|כְּפֶ֣רֶץ\rb*;
\q2 \rb through|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the ruins|שֹׁ֝אָ֗ה\rb* \rb they keep rolling in|הִתְגַּלְגָּֽלוּ׃\rb*.
\s1 Job’s Prosperity Becomes Calamity
\q1 \v 15 \rb Terrors|בַּלָּ֫ה֥וֹת\rb* \rb are turned loose|הָהְפַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֗י\rb*;
\q2 \rb they drive away|תִּרְדֹּ֣ף\rb* \rb my dignity|נְדִבָתִ֑י\rb* \rb as by the wind|כָּ֭רוּחַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my prosperity|יְשֻׁעָתִֽי׃\rb* \rb has passed|עָבְרָ֥ה\rb* \rb like a cloud|וּ֝כְעָ֗ב\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb my soul|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb is poured out|תִּשְׁתַּפֵּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb within me|עָ֭לַי\rb*;
\q2 \rb days|יְמֵי־\rb* \rb of affliction|עֹֽנִי׃\rb* \rb grip me|יֹ֭אחֲז֣וּנִי\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb Night|לַ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb pierces|נִקַּ֣ר\rb*\rb |מֵעָלָ֑י\rb* \rb my bones|עֲ֭צָמַי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my gnawing pains|וְ֝עֹרְקַ֗י\rb* \rb never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb rest|יִשְׁכָּבֽוּן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb With great|בְּרָב־\rb* \rb force|כֹּ֭חַ\rb* \rb He grasps|יִתְחַפֵּ֣שׂ\rb* \rb my garment|לְבוּשִׁ֑י\rb*;\f + \fr 30:18 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa He becomes like a garment to me \ft or \fqa my garment is disfigured\f*
\q2 \rb He seizes me|יַֽאַזְרֵֽנִי׃\rb* \rb by the collar|כְּפִ֖י\rb* \rb of my tunic|כֻתָּנְתִּ֣י\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb He throws me|הֹרָ֥נִי\rb* \rb into the mud|לַחֹ֑מֶר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I have become|וָ֝אֶתְמַשֵּׁ֗ל\rb* \rb like dust|כֶּעָפָ֥ר\rb* \rb and ashes|וָאֵֽפֶר׃\rb*.
