\q1 \rb Let the Almighty|שַׁדַּ֣י\rb* \rb answer me|יַעֲנֵ֑נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb let my accuser|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |רִיבִֽי׃\rb* \rb compose|כָּ֝תַ֗ב\rb* \rb an indictment|וְסֵ֥פֶר\rb*.
\q1 \v 36 \rb Surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb I would carry it|אֶשָּׂאֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my shoulder|שִׁ֭כְמִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and wear|אֶֽעֶנְדֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb it like a crown|עֲטָר֣וֹת\rb*.
\q1 \v 37 \rb I would give|אַגִּידֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb account|מִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of all my steps|צְ֭עָדַי\rb*;
\q2 \rb I would approach Him|אֲקָרֲבֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb like|כְּמוֹ־\rb* \rb a prince|נָ֝גִ֗יד\rb*.)—
\b 
\q1 \v 38 \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb my land|אַדְמָתִ֣י\rb* \rb cries out|תִזְעָ֑ק\rb* \rb against me|עָ֭לַי\rb*
\q2 \rb and its furrows|תְּלָמֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb weep|יִבְכָּיֽוּן׃\rb* \rb together|וְ֝יַ֗חַד\rb*,
\q1 \v 39 \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb I have devoured|אָכַ֣לְתִּי\rb* \rb its produce|כֹּ֭חָהּ\rb* \rb without|בְלִי־\rb* \rb payment|כָ֑סֶף\rb*
\q2 \rb or broken the spirit|וְנֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הִפָּֽחְתִּי׃\rb* \rb of its tenants|בְּעָלֶ֣יהָ\rb*,
\q1 \v 40 \rb then let briers|ח֗וֹחַ\rb* \rb grow|יֵ֥צֵא\rb* \rb instead of|תַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb wheat|חִטָּ֨ה׀\rb*
\q2 \rb and stinkweed|בָאְשָׁ֑ה\rb* \rb instead of|וְתַֽחַת־\rb* \rb barley|שְׂעֹרָ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \rb Thus conclude|תַּ֝֗מּוּ\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Job|אִיּֽוֹב׃פ\rb*.
\c 32
\s1 Elihu Rebukes Job’s Friends
\p \v 1 \rb So these|הָ֭אֵלֶּה\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb stopped|וַֽיִּשְׁבְּת֡וּ\rb* \rb answering|מֵעֲנ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Job|אִיּ֑וֹב\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb was righteous|צַדִּ֣יק\rb* \rb in his own eyes|בְּעֵינָֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb This kindled|וַיִּ֤חַר\rb* \rb the anger|אַ֨ף׀\rb* \rb of Elihu|אֱלִיה֣וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Barachel|בַּרַכְאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb the Buzite|הַבּוּזִי֮\rb*, \rb of the family|מִמִּשְׁפַּ֪חַ֫ת\rb* \rb of Ram|רָ֥ם\rb*. \rb He burned|חָרָ֣ה\rb* \rb with anger|אַפּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb against Job|בְּ֭אִיּוֹב\rb* \rb for|עַֽל־\rb* \rb justifying|צַדְּק֥וֹ\rb* \rb himself|נַ֝פְשׁ֗וֹ\rb* \rb rather than God|מֵאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb and he burned|חָרָ֪ה\rb* \rb with anger|אַ֫פּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb against Job’s three|וּבִשְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb friends|רֵעָיו֮\rb* \rb because|עַ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had failed|לֹא־\rb*\rb |מָצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb to refute Job|מַעֲנֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb and yet had condemned|וַ֝יַּרְשִׁ֗יעוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|אִיּֽוֹב׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Now Elihu|וֶֽאֱלִיה֗וּ\rb* \rb had waited|חִכָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to speak|בִּדְבָרִ֑ים\rb* \rb to Job|אִ֭יּוֹב\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the others|הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb were older|זְֽקֵנִים־\rb* \rb than he|מִמֶּ֣נּוּ\rb*\rb |לְיָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb But when he|אֱלִיה֗וּא\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֘י\rb* \rb the three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb had no|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb further reply|מַעֲנֶ֗ה\rb*\rb |בְּ֭פִי\rb*, \rb his anger|אַפּֽוֹ׃פ\rb* \rb was kindled|וַיִּ֥חַר\rb*. \v 6 \rb So Elihu|אֱלִיה֖וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Barachel|בַּֽרַכְאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb the Buzite|הַבּוּזִ֗י\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֫אמַ֥ר\rb* \rb declared|וַיַּ֤עַן׀\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am young|צָ֘עִ֤יר\rb* \rb in years|לְ֭יָמִים\rb*,
\q2 \rb while you|וְאַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb are old|יְשִׁישִׁ֑ים\rb*;
\q1 \rb that is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb I was timid|זָחַ֥לְתִּי\rb* \rb and afraid|וָֽאִירָ֓א׀\rb*
\q2 \rb to tell you|מֵחַוֺּ֖ת\rb* \rb what I know|דֵּעִ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb I thought|אָ֭מַרְתִּי\rb* \rb that age|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb should speak|יְדַבֵּ֑רוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and many|וְרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb years|שָׁ֝נִ֗ים\rb* \rb should teach|יֹדִ֥יעוּ\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb But|אָ֭כֵן\rb* \rb there is|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb a spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb*\f + \fr 32:8 \ft Or \fqa the Spirit\ft ; similarly in verse 18\f* \rb in a man|בֶאֱנ֑וֹשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb the breath|וְנִשְׁמַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the Almighty|שַׁדַּ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb that gives him understanding|תְּבִינֵֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb It is not only|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb the old|רַבִּ֥ים\rb*\f + \fr 32:9 \ft Or \fqa many \ft or \fqa great\f* \rb who are wise|יֶחְכָּ֑מוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb or the elderly|וּ֝זְקֵנִ֗ים\rb* \rb who understand|יָבִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb I say|אָ֭מַרְתִּי\rb*, ‘\rb Listen|שִׁמְעָה־\rb* \rb to me|לִּ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb too|אַף־\rb* \rb will declare|אֲחַוֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb what I know|דֵּעִ֣י\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Indeed|הֵ֤ן\rb*, \rb I waited|הוֹחַ֨לְתִּי\rb* \rb while you spoke|לְֽדִבְרֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb I listened|אָ֭זִין\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb your reasoning|תְּב֥וּנֹֽתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*;
\q1 \rb as|עַֽד־\rb* \rb you searched|תַּחְקְר֥וּן\rb* \rb for words|מִלִּֽין׃\rb*,
\q2 \v 12 \rb I paid you full attention|אֶתְבּ֫וֹנָ֥ן\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְעָֽדֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb But no one|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb proved Job|לְאִיּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb wrong|מוֹכִ֑יחַ\rb*;
\q2 \rb not one of|מִכֶּֽם׃\rb* \rb you rebutted|עוֹנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb his arguments|אֲמָרָ֣יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb So do not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb claim|תֹּ֣֭אמְרוּ\rb*, ‘\rb We have found|מָצָ֣אנוּ\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb let God|אֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb man|אִֽישׁ׃\rb*, \rb refute him|יִדְּפֶ֣נּוּ\rb*.’
\q1 \v 14 \rb But Job has not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb directed|עָרַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb his words|מִלִּ֑ין\rb* \rb against me|אֵלַ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb answer him|אֲשִׁיבֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb with your arguments|וּ֝בְאִמְרֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb Job’s friends are dismayed|חַ֭תּוּ\rb*, \rb with no|לֹא־\rb* \rb more|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb to say|עָ֣נוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb words|מִלִּֽים׃\rb* \rb have escaped|הֶעְתִּ֖יקוּ\rb* \rb them|מֵהֶ֣ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb Must I wait|וְ֭הוֹחַלְתִּי\rb*, \rb now that|כִּי־\rb* \rb they are silent|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יְדַבֵּ֑רוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb now that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they stand|עָ֝מְד֗וּ\rb* \rb and no|לֹא־\rb* \rb longer|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb reply|עָ֥נוּ\rb*?
\q1 \v 17 \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*\rb |חֶלְקִ֑י\rb* \rb too|אַף־\rb* \rb will answer|אַעֲנֶ֣ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb yes|אַף־\rb*, \rb I|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb will declare|אֲחַוֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb what I know|דֵעִ֣י\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb For|כִּ֭י\rb* \rb I am full of|מָלֵ֣תִי\rb* \rb words|מִלִּ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb within me|בִּטְנִֽי׃\rb* \rb compels me|הֱ֝צִיקַ֗תְנִי\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb Behold|הִנֵּֽה־\rb*, \rb my belly|בִטְנִ֗י\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb is like unvented|יִפָּתֵ֑חַ\rb* \rb wine|כְּיַ֥יִן\rb*;
\q2 \rb it is about to burst|יִבָּקֵֽעַ׃\rb* \rb like a new|חֲ֝דָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb wineskin|כְּאֹב֥וֹת\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb I must speak|אֲדַבְּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb and find relief|וְיִֽרְוַֽח־\rb*;
\q2 \rb I must open|אֶפְתַּ֖ח\rb* \rb my lips|שְׂפָתַ֣י\rb* \rb and respond|וְאֶֽעֱנֶֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb I will be partial|אֶשָּׂ֣א\rb*\rb |פְנֵי־\rb* \rb to no|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֭א\rb* \rb one|אִ֑ישׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb*
\q2 \rb nor will|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb I flatter|אֲכַנֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb any man|אָ֝דָ֗ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know how|יָדַ֣עְתִּי\rb* \rb to flatter|אֲכַנֶּ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb or my Maker|עֹשֵֽׂנִי׃\rb* \rb would remove me|יִשָּׂאֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb in an instant|כִּ֝מְעַ֗ט\rb*.[’’]
\c 33
\s1 Elihu Rebukes Job
\q1 \v 1 “\rb But|וְֽאוּלָ֗ם\rb* \rb now|נָ֣א\rb*, \rb O Job|אִיּ֣וֹב\rb*, \rb hear|שְׁמַֽע־\rb* \rb my speech|מִלָּ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and listen|הַאֲזִֽינָה׃\rb* \rb to all|וְֽכָל־\rb* \rb my words|דְּבָרַ֥י\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb Behold|הִנֵּה־\rb*\rb |נָ֭א\rb*, \rb I will open|פָּתַ֣חְתִּי\rb* \rb my mouth|פִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb my address|דִּבְּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb is on the tip|בְחִכִּֽי׃\rb* \rb of my tongue|לְשׁוֹנִ֣י\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb My words|אֲמָרָ֑י\rb* \rb are from an upright|יֹֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb heart|לִבִּ֥י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and my lips|שְׂ֝פָתַ֗י\rb* \rb speak|מִלֵּֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb sincerely|בָּר֥וּר\rb* \rb what I know|וְדַ֥עַת\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb The Spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of God|אֵ֥ל\rb* \rb has made me|עָשָׂ֑תְנִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the breath|וְנִשְׁמַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the Almighty|שַׁדַּ֣י\rb* \rb gives me life|תְּחַיֵּֽנִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb Refute me|הֲשִׁיבֵ֑נִי\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you can|תּוּכַ֥ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb prepare your case|עֶרְכָ֥ה\rb* \rb and confront me|לְ֝פָנַ֗י\rb*\rb |הִתְיַצָּֽבָה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb |הֵן־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*\rb |כְפִ֣יךָ\rb* \rb am just like you before God|לָאֵ֑ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb I|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb was also|גַם־\rb* \rb formed|קֹרַ֥צְתִּי\rb* \rb from clay|מֵ֝חֹ֗מֶר\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb Surely|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb fear of me|אֵ֭מָתִי\rb* \rb should terrify you|תְבַעֲתֶ֑ךָּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb nor|לֹא־\rb* \rb will my hand|וְ֝אַכְפִּ֗י\rb* \rb be heavy|יִכְבָּֽד׃\rb* \rb upon you|עָלֶ֥יךָ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Surely|אַ֭ךְ\rb* \rb you have spoken|אָמַ֣רְתָּ\rb* \rb in my hearing|בְאָזְנָ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb |וְק֖וֹל\rb* \rb and I have heard|אֶשְׁמָֽע׃\rb* \rb these very words|מִלִּ֣ין\rb*:
\q1 \v 9 ‘\rb I|אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb am pure|זַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb without|בְּֽלִ֫י\rb* \rb transgression|פָ֥שַׁע\rb*;
\q2 \rb I|אָנֹכִ֑י\rb* \rb am clean|חַ֥ף\rb*, \rb with no|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb iniquity|עָוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb in me|לִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Yet|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb God finds|יִמְצָ֑א\rb* \rb occasions|תְּ֭נוּאוֹת\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֣י\rb*;
\q2 \rb He counts me|יַחְשְׁבֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb as His|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb enemy|לְאוֹיֵ֣ב\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb He puts|יָשֵׂ֣ם\rb* \rb my feet|רַגְלָ֑י\rb* \rb in the stocks|בַּסַּ֣ד\rb*;
\q2 \rb He watches over|יִ֝שְׁמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my paths|אָרְחֹתָֽי׃\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb Behold|הֶן־\rb*, \rb you are not|לֹא־\rb* \rb right|צָדַ֣קְתָּ\rb* \rb in this matter|זֹ֣את\rb*.
\q2 \rb I will answer you|אֶעֱנֶ֑ךָּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֱ֝ל֗וֹהַ\rb* \rb is greater|יִרְבֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb than man|מֵאֱנֽוֹשׁ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb Why|מַ֭דּוּעַ\rb* \rb do you complain|רִיב֑וֹתָ\rb* \rb to Him|אֵלָ֣יו\rb*
\q2 \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb He answers|יַעֲנֶֽה׃\rb* \rb nothing|לֹ֣א־\rb*\rb |כָל־\rb* \rb a man asks|דְּ֝בָרָ֗יו\rb*?\f + \fr 33:13 \ft Or \fqa that He answers for none of His actions\f*
\q1 \v 14 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb speaks|יְדַבֶּר־\rb* \rb in one way|בְאַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb and in another|וּ֝בִשְׁתַּ֗יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb yet no one|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb notices|יְשׁוּרֶֽנָּה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb In a dream|בַּחֲל֤וֹם׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb in a vision|חֶזְי֬וֹן\rb* \rb in the night|לַ֗יְלָה\rb*,
\q1 \rb when deep sleep|תַּ֭רְדֵּמָה\rb* \rb falls|בִּנְפֹ֣ל\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb as they slumber|בִּ֝תְנוּמ֗וֹת\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵ֣י\rb* \rb their beds|מִשְׁכָּֽב׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 16 \rb |אָ֣ז\rb* \rb He opens|יִ֭גְלֶה\rb* \rb their ears|אֹ֣זֶן\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and terrifies them|יַחְתֹּֽם׃\rb* \rb with warnings|וּבְמֹ֖סָרָ֣ם\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb to turn|לְ֭הָסִיר\rb* \rb a man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb from wrongdoing|מַעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and keep him|יְכַסֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb from|מִגֶּ֣בֶר\rb* \rb pride|וְגֵוָ֖ה\rb*,
\q1 \v 18 \rb to preserve|יַחְשֹׂ֣ךְ\rb* \rb his soul|נַ֭פְשׁוֹ\rb* \rb from|מִנִּי־\rb* \rb the Pit|שָׁ֑חַת\rb*
\q2 \rb and his life|וְ֝חַיָּת֗וֹ\rb* \rb from perishing|מֵעֲבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּשָּֽׁלַח׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb A man is also chastened|וְהוּכַ֣ח\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his bed|מִשְׁכָּב֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb with pain|בְּ֭מַכְאוֹב\rb* \rb and constant|אֵתָֽן׃\rb* \rb distress|וְרִיב\rb* \rb in his bones|עֲצָמָ֣יו\rb*,
\q1 \v 20 \rb so that he|חַיָּת֣וֹ\rb* \rb detests|וְזִֽהֲמַ֣תּוּ\rb* \rb his bread|לָ֑חֶם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and his soul|וְ֝נַפְשׁ֗וֹ\rb* \rb loathes his favorite|תַּאֲוָֽה׃\rb* \rb food|מַאֲכַ֥ל\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb His flesh|בְּשָׂר֣וֹ\rb* \rb wastes away|יִ֣כֶל\rb* \rb from sight|מֵרֹ֑אִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and his hidden|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |רֻאּֽוּ׃\rb* \rb bones|עַ֝צְמוֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb protrude|וּשְׁפִי\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb He|נַפְשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb draws near|וַתִּקְרַ֣ב\rb* \rb to the Pit|לַשַּׁ֣חַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and his life|וְ֝חַיָּת֗וֹ\rb* \rb to the messengers of death|לַֽמְמִתִֽים׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 23 \rb Yet if|אִם־\rb* \rb there is|יֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb a messenger|מַלְאָ֗ךְ\rb* \rb on his side|עָלָ֨יו׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb mediator|מֵלִ֗יץ\rb* \rb in|מִנִּי־\rb* \rb a thousand|אָ֑לֶף\rb*,
\q1 \rb to tell|לְהַגִּ֖יד\rb* \rb a man|לְאָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb what is right for him|יָשְׁרֽוֹ׃\rb*,
\q2 \v 24 \rb to be gracious|וַיְחֻנֶּ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb to him and say|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*,
\q1 ‘\rb Spare him|פְּ֭דָעֵהוּ\rb* \rb from going down|מֵרֶ֥דֶת\rb* \rb to the Pit|שָׁ֗חַת\rb*;
\q2 \rb I have found|מָצָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb his ransom|כֹֽפֶר׃\rb*,’
\q1 \v 25 \rb then his flesh|בְּשָׂר֣וֹ\rb* \rb is refreshed|רֻֽטֲפַ֣שׁ\rb* \rb like a child’s|מִנֹּ֑עַר\rb*;
\q2 \rb he returns|יָ֝שׁ֗וּב\rb* \rb to the days|לִימֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his youth|עֲלוּמָֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb He prays|יֶעְתַּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|אֱל֨וֹהַּ׀\rb* \rb and finds favor|וַיִּרְצֵ֗הוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb he sees|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb God’s face|פָּ֭נָיו\rb* \rb and shouts for joy|בִּתְרוּעָ֑ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb and God restores|וַיָּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb His righteousness|צִדְקָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q2 \rb to that man|לֶ֝אֱנ֗וֹשׁ\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb Then he sings|יָשֹׁ֤ר׀\rb* \rb before|עַל־\rb*\f + \fr 33:27 \ft Or \fqa Then he looks upon\f* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb with these words|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*:
\q1 ‘\rb I have sinned|חָ֭טָאתִי\rb* \rb and perverted|הֶעֱוֵ֗יתִי\rb* \rb what was right|וְיָשָׁ֥ר\rb*;
\q2 \rb yet I did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb get what I deserved|שָׁ֥וָה\rb*.
\q1 \v 28 \rb He redeemed|פָּדָ֣ה\rb* \rb my soul|נַפְשִׁי\rb* \rb from going down|מֵעֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb to the Pit|בַּשָּׁ֑חַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I will live|וְחַיָּתִי\rb* \rb to see|תִּרְאֶֽה׃\rb* \rb the light|בָּא֥וֹר\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 29 \rb Behold|הֶן־\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these things|אֵ֭לֶּה\rb* \rb God|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb does|יִפְעַל־\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb a man|גָּֽבֶר׃\rb*,
\q2 \rb two|פַּעֲמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb or even three times|שָׁל֣וֹשׁ\rb*,
\q1 \v 30 \rb to bring back|לְהָשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb his soul|נַ֭פְשׁוֹ\rb* \rb from|מִנִּי־\rb* \rb the Pit|שָׁ֑חַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb that he may be enlightened|לֵ֝א֗וֹר\rb* \rb with the light|בְּא֣וֹר\rb* \rb of life|הַֽחַיִּים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 31 \rb Pay attention|הַקְשֵׁ֖ב\rb*, \rb Job|אִיּ֥וֹב\rb*, \rb and listen|שְֽׁמַֽע־\rb* \rb to me|לִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb be silent|הַ֝חֲרֵ֗שׁ\rb*, \rb and I|וְאָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb will speak|אֲדַבֵּֽר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 32 \rb But if|אִם־\rb* \rb you have|יֵשׁ־\rb* \rb something to say|מִלִּ֥ין\rb*, \rb answer me|הֲשִׁיבֵ֑נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb speak up|דַּ֝בֵּ֗ר\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I would like|חָפַ֥צְתִּי\rb* \rb to vindicate you|צַדְּקֶֽךָּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 33 \rb But if|אִם־\rb* \rb not|אַ֭יִן\rb*,\rb |אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb then listen|שְֽׁמַֽע־\rb* \rb to me|לִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb be quiet|הַ֝חֲרֵ֗שׁ\rb*, \rb and I will teach|וַאֲאַלֶּפְךָ֥\rb* \rb you wisdom|חָכְמָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\c 34
\s1 Elihu Confirms God’s Justice
\p \v 1 \rb Then Elihu|אֱלִיה֗וּא\rb* \rb continued|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb Hear|שִׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb my words|מִלָּ֑י\rb*, \rb O wise men|חֲכָמִ֣ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb give ear|הַאֲזִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb to me|לִֽי׃\rb*, \rb O men of learning|וְ֝יֹדְעִ֗ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb the ear|אֹ֭זֶן\rb* \rb tests|תִּבְחָ֑ן\rb* \rb words|מִלִּ֣ין\rb*
\q2 \rb as the mouth|וְ֝חֵ֗ךְ\rb* \rb tastes|יִטְעַ֥ם\rb* \rb food|לֶאֱכֹֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb Let us choose|נִבְחֲרָה־\rb* \rb for ourselves|לָּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb what is right|מִשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb*;
\q2 \rb let us learn|נֵדְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb together|בֵינֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb is good|טּֽוֹב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Job|אִיּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb has declared|אָ֭מַר\rb*, ‘\rb I am righteous|צָדַ֑קְתִּי\rb*,
\q2 \rb yet God|וְ֝אֵ֗ל\rb* \rb has deprived me of|הֵסִ֥יר\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּטִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Would I lie|אֲכַזֵּ֑ב\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb my case|מִשְׁפָּטִ֥י\rb*?
\q2 \rb My wound|חִצִּ֣י\rb* \rb is incurable|אָנ֖וּשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb though I am without|בְלִי־\rb* \rb transgression|פָֽשַׁע׃\rb*.’
\q1 \v 7 \rb What|מִי־\rb* \rb man|גֶ֥בֶר\rb* \rb is like Job|כְּאִיּ֑וֹב\rb*,
\q2 \rb who drinks up|יִֽשְׁתֶּה־\rb* \rb derision|לַּ֥עַג\rb* \rb like water|כַּמָּֽיִם׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 8 \rb He keeps|וְאָרַ֣ח\rb* \rb company|לְ֭חֶבְרָה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb evildoers|פֹּ֣עֲלֵי\rb*\rb |אָ֑וֶן\rb*
\q2 \rb and walks|וְ֝לָלֶ֗כֶת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb wicked|רֶֽשַׁע׃\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁי־\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he has said|אָ֭מַר\rb*, ‘\rb It profits|יִסְכָּן־\rb* \rb a man|גָּ֑בֶר\rb* \rb nothing|לֹ֣א\rb*
\q2 \rb that he should delight|בִּ֝רְצֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֤ן׀\rb* \rb listen|שִׁמְע֫וּ\rb* \rb to me|לִ֥י\rb*,
\q2 \rb O men|אַ֥נֲשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of understanding|לֵבָ֗ב\rb*.
\q1 \rb Far be it|חָלִ֖לָה\rb* \rb from God|לָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb to do wrong|מֵרֶ֗שַׁע\rb*,
\q2 \rb and from the Almighty|וְשַׁדַּ֥י\rb* \rb to act unjustly|מֵעָֽוֶל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אָ֭דָם\rb* \rb according to a man’s deeds|פֹ֣עַל\rb* \rb He repays|יְשַׁלֶּם־\rb* \rb him|ל֑וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb according to a man’s|אִ֝֗ישׁ\rb* \rb ways|וּֽכְאֹ֥רַח\rb* \rb He brings consequences|יַמְצִאֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb Indeed|אַף־\rb*, \rb it is true|אָמְנָ֗ם\rb* \rb that God|אֵ֥ל\rb* \rb does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb act wickedly|יַרְשִׁ֑יעַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the Almighty|וְ֝שַׁדַּ֗י\rb* \rb does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb pervert|יְעַוֵּ֥ת\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb gave Him charge|פָקַ֣ד\rb* \rb over the earth|אָ֑רְצָה\rb*?
\q2 \rb Who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb appointed Him|שָׂ֝֗ם\rb* \rb over the whole|כֻּלָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb world|תֵּבֵ֥ל\rb*?
\q1 \v 14 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb He were to set|יָשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb His heart|לִבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb to it|אֵלָ֣יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and withdraw|יֶאֱסֹֽף׃\rb* \rb His Spirit|רוּח֥וֹ\rb* \rb and breath|וְ֝נִשְׁמָת֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֥יו\rb*,
\q1 \v 15 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb flesh|בָּשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb would perish|יִגְוַ֣ע\rb* \rb together|יָ֑חַד\rb*
\q2 \rb and mankind|וְ֝אָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb would return|יָשֽׁוּב׃\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the dust|עָפָ֥ר\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you have understanding|בִּ֥ינָה\rb*, \rb hear|שִׁמְעָה־\rb* \rb this|זֹּ֑את\rb*;
\q2 \rb listen to|הַ֝אֲזִ֗ינָה\rb*\rb |לְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb my words|מִלָּֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb Could|הַאַ֬ף\rb* \rb one who hates|שׂוֹנֵ֣א\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּ֣ט\rb* \rb govern|יַחֲב֑וֹשׁ\rb*?
\q2 \rb |וְאִם־\rb* \rb Will you condemn|תַּרְשִֽׁיעַ׃\rb* \rb the just|צַדִּ֖יק\rb* \rb and mighty One|כַּבִּ֣יר\rb*,
\q1 \v 18 \rb who says|הַאֲמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb to kings|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*, ‘\rb You are worthless|בְּלִיָּ֑עַל\rb*!’
\q2 \rb and to|אֶל־\rb* \rb nobles|נְדִיבִֽים׃\rb*, ‘\rb You are wicked|רָ֝שָׁ֗ע\rb*,’
\q1 \v 19 \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb partial|נָשָׂ֨א׀\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb to princes|שָׂרִ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and does not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb favor|נִכַּר־\rb* \rb rich|שׁ֭וֹעַ\rb* \rb over|לִפְנֵי־\rb* \rb poor|דָ֑ל\rb*?
\q2 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they are all|כֻּלָּֽם׃\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb of His hands|יָדָ֣יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb They die|יָמֻתוּ֮\rb* \rb in an instant|רֶ֤גַע׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb in the middle|וַחֲצ֪וֹת\rb* \rb of the night|לָ֥יְלָה\rb*.
\q1 \rb The people|עָ֣ם\rb* \rb convulse|יְגֹעֲשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb and pass away|וְיַעֲבֹ֑רוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb the mighty|אַ֝בִּ֗יר\rb* \rb are removed|וְיָסִ֥ירוּ\rb* \rb without|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb human hand|בְיָֽד׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb His eyes are|עֵ֭ינָיו\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ways|דַּרְכֵי־\rb* \rb of a man|אִ֑ישׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and He sees|יִרְאֶֽה׃\rb*\rb |וְֽכָל־\rb* \rb his every step|צְעָדָ֥יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb There is no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb darkness|חֹ֭שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb or|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb deep shadow|צַלְמָ֑וֶת\rb*
\q2 \rb where|שָׁ֝֗ם\rb* \rb the workers|פֹּ֣עֲלֵי\rb* \rb of iniquity|אָֽוֶן׃\rb* \rb can hide|לְהִסָּ֥תֶר\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb God|אֵ֝֗ל\rb* \rb need not|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb examine|יָשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb a man|אִ֭ישׁ\rb* \rb further|ע֑וֹד\rb*
\q2 \rb or have him approach|לַהֲלֹ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb for judgment|בַּמִּשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb He shatters|יָרֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb the mighty|כַּבִּירִ֣ים\rb* \rb without|לֹא־\rb* \rb inquiry|חֵ֑קֶר\rb*
\q2 \rb and sets up|וַיַּעֲמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb others|אֲחֵרִ֣ים\rb* \rb in their place|תַּחְתָּֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb He recognizes|יַ֭כִּיר\rb* \rb their deeds|מַעְבָּֽדֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb He overthrows them|וְהָ֥פַךְ\rb* \rb in the night|לַ֝֗יְלָה\rb* \rb and they are crushed|וְיִדַּכָּֽאוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb He strikes them|סְפָקָ֗ם\rb* \rb for|תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb their wickedness|רְשָׁעִ֥ים\rb*
\q2 \rb in full|בִּמְק֥וֹם\rb* \rb view|רֹאִֽים׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 27 \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֭ן\rb* \rb they turned aside|סָ֣רוּ\rb* \rb from Him|מֵֽאַחֲרָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and had no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb regard|הִשְׂכִּֽילוּ׃\rb* \rb for any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of His ways|דְּ֝רָכָ֗יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 28 \rb They caused the cry|צַֽעֲקַת־\rb* \rb of the poor|דָּ֑ל\rb* \rb to come|לְהָבִ֣יא\rb* \rb before Him|עָ֭לָיו\rb*,
\q2 \rb and He heard|יִשְׁמָֽע׃\rb* \rb the outcry|וְצַעֲקַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the afflicted|עֲנִיִּ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 29 \rb But when He|וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb remains silent|יַשְׁקִ֨ט׀\rb*, \rb who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb can condemn Him|יַרְשִׁ֗עַ\rb*?
\q2 \rb When He hides|וְיַסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb His face|פָּ֭נִים\rb*, \rb who|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb can see Him|יְשׁוּרֶ֑נּוּ\rb*?
\q1 \rb Yet He watches over|וְעַל־\rb* \rb both|יָֽחַד׃\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb and nation|גּ֖וֹי\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb*,
\q2 \v 30 \rb that godless|חָנֵ֗ף\rb* \rb men|אָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb should not rule|מִ֭מְּלֹךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb or lay snares|מִמֹּ֥קְשֵׁי\rb* \rb for the people|עָֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 31 \rb Suppose|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb someone says|הֶאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|אֵ֭ל\rb*,
\q2 ‘\rb I have endured my punishment|נָשָׂ֗אתִי\rb*; \rb I will offend|אֶחְבֹּֽל׃\rb* \rb no more|לֹ֣א\rb*.
\q1 \v 32 \rb Teach me|הֹרֵ֑נִי\rb* \rb what I cannot|בִּלְעֲדֵ֣י\rb* \rb see|אֶ֭חֱזֶה\rb*;\rb |אַתָּ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb if|אִֽם־\rb* \rb I have done|פָּ֝עַ֗לְתִּי\rb* \rb wrong|עָ֥וֶל\rb*, \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do it again|אֹסִֽיף׃\rb*.’
\q1 \v 33 \rb Should God repay you|יְשַׁלְמֶ֨נָּה\rb* \rb on your own terms|הַֽמֵעִמְּךָ֬\rb*
\q2 \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have disavowed Him|מָאַ֗סְתָּ\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb*?
\q1 \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb must choose|תִבְחַ֣ר\rb*, \rb not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb I|אָ֑נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb so tell me|דַבֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb what|וּֽמַה־\rb* \rb you know|יָדַ֥עְתָּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 34 \rb Men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of understanding|לֵ֭בָב\rb* \rb will declare|יֹ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb to me|לִ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the wise|חָ֝כָ֗ם\rb* \rb men|וְגֶ֥בֶר\rb* \rb who hear me|שֹׁמֵ֥עַֽ\rb* \rb will say|לִֽי׃\rb*:
\q1 \v 35 ‘\rb Job|אִ֭יּוֹב\rb* \rb speaks|יְדַבֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb without|לֹא־\rb* \rb knowledge|בְדַ֣עַת\rb*;
\q2 \rb his words|וּ֝דְבָרָ֗יו\rb* \rb lack|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb insight|בְהַשְׂכֵּֽיל׃\rb*.’
\q1 \v 36 \rb If only|אָבִ֗י\rb* \rb Job|אִיּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb were tried|יִבָּחֵ֣ן\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the utmost|נֶ֑צַח\rb*
\q2 \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb answering|תְּ֝שֻׁבֹ֗ת\rb* \rb like a wicked|אָֽוֶן׃\rb* \rb man|בְּאַנְשֵׁי־\rb*.
\q1 \v 37 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he adds|יֹ֘סִ֤יף\rb* \rb rebellion|פֶ֭שַׁע\rb* \rb to|עַֽל־\rb* \rb his sin|חַטָּאת֣וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb he claps his hands|יִסְפּ֑וֹק\rb* \rb among us|בֵּינֵ֣ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and multiplies|וְיֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb his words|אֲמָרָ֣יו\rb* \rb against God|לָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.”
\c 35
\s1 Elihu Recalls God’s Justice
\p \v 1 \rb And Elihu|אֱלִיה֗וּ\rb* \rb went on|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb* \rb to say|וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb Do you think|חָשַׁ֣בְתָּ\rb* \rb this|הֲ֭זֹאת\rb* \rb is just|לְמִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb*?
\q2 \rb You say|אָ֝מַ֗רְתָּ\rb*, ‘\rb I am more righteous|צִדְקִ֥י\rb* \rb than God|מֵאֵֽל׃\rb*.’\f + \fr 35:2 \ft Or \fqa ‘I am righteous before God.’\f*
\q1 \v 3 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you ask|תֹ֭אמַר\rb*, ‘\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb does it profit|יִּסְכָּן־\rb* \rb me|לָ֑ךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and what|מָֽה־\rb* \rb benefit do I gain|אֹ֝עִ֗יל\rb* \rb apart from sin|מֵֽחַטָּאתִֽי׃\rb*?’
\q1 \v 4 \rb I|אֲ֭נִי\rb* \rb will reply|אֲשִֽׁיבְךָ֣\rb* \rb to you|מִלִּ֑ין\rb*\rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb and to your friends|רֵעֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb as well|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb Look|הַבֵּ֣ט\rb* \rb to the heavens|שָׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb and see|וּרְאֵ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb gaze|וְשׁ֥וּר\rb* \rb at the clouds|שְׁ֝חָקִ֗ים\rb* \rb high|גָּבְה֥וּ\rb* \rb above you|מִמֶּֽךָּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you sin|חָ֭טָאתָ\rb*, \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb do you accomplish|תִּפְעָל־\rb* \rb against Him|בּ֑וֹ\rb*?
\q2 \rb If you multiply|וְרַבּ֥וּ\rb* \rb your transgressions|פְ֝שָׁעֶ֗יךָ\rb*, \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb do you do|תַּעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb to Him|לּֽוֹ׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 7 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you are righteous|צָ֭דַקְתָּ\rb*, \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb do you give|תִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb Him|ל֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb does He receive|יִקָּֽח׃\rb* \rb from your hand|מִיָּדְךָ֥\rb*?
\q1 \v 8 \rb Your wickedness|רִשְׁעֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb affects only a man|לְאִישׁ־\rb* \rb like yourself|כָּמ֥וֹךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and your righteousness|צִדְקָתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb only a son|וּלְבֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָ֝דָ֗ם\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb Men cry out|יַזְעִ֑יקוּ\rb* \rb under great|מֵ֭רֹב\rb* \rb oppression|עֲשׁוּקִ֣ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb they plead for relief|יְשַׁוְּע֖וּ\rb* \rb from the arm|מִזְּר֣וֹעַ\rb* \rb of the mighty|רַבִּֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb But no|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb one asks|אָמַ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb Where is|אַ֭יֵּה\rb* \rb God|אֱל֣וֹהַּ\rb* \rb my Maker|עֹשָׂ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb who gives us|נֹתֵ֖ן\rb* \rb songs|זְמִר֣וֹת\rb* \rb in the night|בַּלָּֽיְלָה׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 11 \rb who teaches us|מַ֭לְּפֵנוּ\rb* \rb more than the beasts|מִבַּהֲמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the earth|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and makes us wiser|יְחַכְּמֵֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb than the birds|וּמֵע֖וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb*?’
\q1 \v 12 \rb There|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb they cry out|יִ֭צְעֲקוּ\rb*, \rb but He does not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb answer|יַעֲנֶ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb because of|מִ֝פְּנֵ֗י\rb* \rb the pride|גְּא֣וֹן\rb* \rb of evil men|רָעִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb Surely|אַךְ־\rb* \rb God|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמַ֥ע׀\rb* \rb to empty pleas|שָׁ֭וְא\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the Almighty|וְ֝שַׁדַּ֗י\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb take note of it|יְשׁוּרֶֽנָּה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb How much less|אַ֣ף\rb*, \rb then, when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you say|תֹ֭אמַר\rb* \rb that you do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb see Him|תְשׁוּרֶ֑נּוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb that your case|דִּ֥ין\rb* \rb is before Him|לְ֝פָנָ֗יו\rb* \rb and you must wait|וּתְח֥וֹלֵֽל\rb* \rb for Him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 15 \rb and further|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb in His anger|אַפּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |אַ֭יִן\rb* \rb He has not punished|פָּקַ֣ד\rb*
\q2 \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb taken much notice|יָדַ֖ע\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb of folly|בַּפַּ֣שׁ\rb*!
\q1 \v 16 \rb So Job|וְ֭אִיּוֹב\rb* \rb opens|יִפְצֶה־\rb* \rb his mouth|פִּ֑יהוּ\rb* \rb in vain|הֶ֣בֶל\rb*
\q2 \rb and multiplies|יַכְבִּֽר׃פ\rb* \rb words|מִלִּ֥ין\rb* \rb without|בִּבְלִי־\rb* \rb knowledge|דַ֝֗עַת\rb*.”
\c 36
\s1 Elihu Describes God’s Power
\p \v 1 \rb And Elihu|אֱלִיה֗וּא\rb* \rb continued|וַיֹּ֥סֶף\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַֽר׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 “\rb Bear|כַּתַּר־\rb* \rb with me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb a little longer|זְ֭עֵיר\rb*, \rb and I will show you|וַאֲחַוֶּ֑ךָּ\rb*
\q2 \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb there is more|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb to be said|מִלִּֽים׃\rb* \rb on God’s behalf|לֶאֱל֣וֹהַּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb I get|אֶשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb my knowledge|דֵ֭עִי\rb* \rb from afar|לְמֵרָח֑וֹק\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I will ascribe|אֶֽתֵּֽן־\rb* \rb justice|צֶֽדֶק׃\rb* \rb to my Maker|וּ֝לְפֹעֲלִ֗י\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb truly|אָ֭מְנָם\rb* \rb my words|מִלָּ֑י\rb* \rb are free of|לֹא־\rb* \rb falsehood|שֶׁ֣קֶר\rb*;
\q2 \rb one perfect|תְּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb in knowledge|דֵּע֣וֹת\rb* \rb is with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb Indeed|הֶן־\rb*, \rb God is|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb mighty|כַּ֭בִּיר\rb*, \rb but He despises|יִמְאָ֑ס\rb* \rb no one|וְלֹ֣א\rb*;
\q2 \rb He is mighty|כַּ֝בִּ֗יר\rb* \rb in strength|כֹּ֣חַֽ\rb* \rb of understanding|לֵֽב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb He does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb keep the wicked|רָשָׁ֑ע\rb* \rb alive|יְחַיֶּ֥ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but He grants|יִתֵּֽן׃\rb* \rb justice|וּמִשְׁפַּ֖ט\rb* \rb to the afflicted|עֲנִיִּ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb He does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb take|יִגְרַ֥ע\rb* \rb His eyes|עֵ֫ינָ֥יו\rb* \rb off the righteous|מִצַּדִּ֗יק\rb*,
\q2 \rb but He enthrones them|לַכִּסֵּ֑א\rb*\rb |וַיֹּשִׁיבֵ֥ם\rb* \rb with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb kings|מְלָכִ֥ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and exalts them|וַיִּגְבָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb forever|לָ֝נֶ֗צַח\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb men are bound|אֲסוּרִ֥ים\rb* \rb with chains|בַּזִּקִּ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb caught|יִ֝לָּכְד֗וּן\rb* \rb in cords|בְּחַבְלֵי־\rb* \rb of affliction|עֹֽנִי׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 9 \rb then He tells|וַיַּגֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb their deeds|פָּעֳלָ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and how|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb arrogantly|יִתְגַּבָּֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb they have transgressed|וּ֝פִשְׁעֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb He opens|וַיִּ֣גֶל\rb* \rb their ears|אָ֭זְנָם\rb* \rb to correction|לַמּוּסָ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and commands|וַ֝יֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they turn|יְשֻׁב֥וּן\rb* \rb from iniquity|מֵאָֽוֶן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb If|אִֽם־\rb* \rb they obey|יִשְׁמְע֗וּ\rb* \rb and serve Him|וְֽיַ֫עֲבֹ֥דוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb then they end|יְכַלּ֣וּ\rb* \rb their days|יְמֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb in prosperity|בַּטּ֑וֹב\rb*
\q2 \rb and their years|וּ֝שְׁנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb in happiness|בַּנְּעִימִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb they do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb obey|יִ֭שְׁמְעוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb then they perish|יַעֲבֹ֑רוּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בְּשֶׁ֣לַח\rb*\f + \fr 36:12 \ft Or \fqa they will cross the river of death\f*
\q2 \rb and die|וְ֝יִגְוְע֗וּ\rb* \rb without|כִּבְלִי־\rb* \rb knowledge|דָֽעַת׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb The godless|וְֽחַנְפֵי־\rb* \rb in heart|לֵ֭ב\rb* \rb harbor|יָשִׂ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb resentment|אָ֑ף\rb*;
\q2 \rb even when|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He binds them|אֲסָרָֽם׃\rb*, \rb they do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb cry for help|יְ֝שַׁוְּע֗וּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb They|נַפְשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb die|תָּמֹ֣ת\rb* \rb in their youth|בַּנֹּ֣עַר\rb*,
\q2 \rb |וְ֝חַיָּתָ֗ם\rb* \rb among the male shrine prostitutes|בַּקְּדֵשִֽׁים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb God rescues|יְחַלֵּ֣ץ\rb* \rb the afflicted|עָנִ֣י\rb* \rb by their affliction|בְעָנְי֑וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 36:15 \ft Or \fqa in their affliction\f*
\q2 \rb and opens|וְיִ֖גֶל\rb* \rb their ears|אָזְנָֽם׃\rb* \rb in oppression|בַּלַּ֣חַץ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb Indeed|וְאַ֤ף\rb*, \rb He drew you|הֲסִיתְךָ֨׀\rb* \rb from the jaws|מִפִּי־\rb* \rb of distress|צָ֗ר\rb*
\q2 \rb to a spacious|לֹא־\rb*\rb |מוּצָ֣ק\rb*\rb |תַּחְתֶּ֑יהָ\rb*\rb |וְנַ֥חַת\rb* \rb and broad place|רַ֭חַב\rb*,
\q2 \rb to a table|שֻׁ֝לְחָנְךָ֗\rb* \rb full|מָ֣לֵא\rb* \rb of richness|דָֽשֶׁן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb But now you are laden|מָלֵ֑אתָ\rb* \rb with the judgment|וְדִין־\rb* \rb due the wicked|רָשָׁ֥ע\rb*;
\q2 \rb judgment|דִּ֖ין\rb* \rb and justice|וּמִשְׁפָּ֣ט\rb* \rb have seized you|יִתְמֹֽכוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Be careful|חֵ֭מָה\rb* \rb that no one|פֶּן־\rb* \rb lures|יְסִֽיתְךָ֣\rb* \rb you with riches|בְסָ֑פֶק\rb*;
\q2 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let a large|וְרָב־\rb* \rb bribe|כֹּ֝֗פֶר\rb* \rb lead you astray|יַטֶּֽךָּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb Can your wealth|שׁ֭וּעֲךָ\rb*\f + \fr 36:19 \ft Or \fqa your cry for help\f* \rb or all|וְ֝כֹ֗ל\rb* \rb your mighty effort|מַאֲמַצֵּי־\rb*\rb |כֹֽחַ׃\rb*
\q2 \rb keep|הֲיַעֲרֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb you from|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb distress|בְצָ֑ר\rb*?
\q1 \v 20 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb long for|תִּשְׁאַ֥ף\rb* \rb the night|הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb when people|עַמִּ֣ים\rb* \rb vanish|לַעֲל֖וֹת\rb* \rb from their homes|תַּחְתָּֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb Be careful|הִ֭שָּׁמֶר\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb to turn|תֵּ֣פֶן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb iniquity|אָ֑וֶן\rb*,
