\s1 The LORD Blesses Job
\p \v 10 \rb After Job|אִיּ֔וֹב\rb* \rb had prayed|בְּהִֽתְפַּֽלְל֖וֹ\rb* \rb for|בְּעַ֣ד\rb* \rb his friends|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb restored|שָׁ֚ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his prosperity|שְׁבִית\rb* \rb and doubled|וַ֧יֹּסֶף\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לְמִשְׁנֶֽה׃\rb* \rb his|לְאִיּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb former possessions|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*. \v 11 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֨יו\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb sisters|אַחְיֹתָיו\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb and prior|לְפָנִ֗ים\rb* \rb acquaintances|יֹדְעָ֣יו\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb and dined|וַיֹּאכְל֨וּ\rb*\rb |לֶחֶם֮\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb in his house|בְּבֵיתוֹ֒\rb*. \rb They consoled|וַיָּנֻ֤דוּ\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb and comforted|וַיְנַחֲמ֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb over|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the adversity|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had brought|הֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָ֑יו\rb*. \rb And each|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb one gave|וַיִּתְּנוּ־\rb* \rb him|ל֗וֹ\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֔ת\rb*\rb |וְאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb piece of silver|קְשִׂיטָ֣ה\rb*\f + \fr 42:11 \ft Hebrew \fqa a kesitah\ft ; the value or weight of the kesitah is no longer known.\f* \rb and a|אֶחָֽד׃ס\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb ring|נֶ֥זֶם\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb So the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb blessed|בֵּרַ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Job’s|אִיּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb latter days|אַחֲרִ֥ית\rb* \rb more than his first|מֵרֵאשִׁת֑וֹ\rb*. \rb He owned|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb 14,000|אַרְבָּעָה֩\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֶ֜לֶף\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֗אן\rb*, \rb 6,000|וְשֵׁ֤שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb camels|גְּמַלִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb 1,000|וְאֶֽלֶף־\rb* \rb yoke|צֶ֥מֶד\rb* \rb of oxen|בָּקָ֖ר\rb*, \rb and 1,000|וְאֶ֥לֶף\rb* \rb female donkeys|אֲתוֹנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb And he also had|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֥נָה\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and three|וְשָׁל֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb daughters|בָּנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb He named|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |שֵׁם־\rb* \rb his first|הָֽאַחַת֙\rb* \rb daughter Jemimah|יְמִימָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb his second|הַשֵּׁנִ֖ית\rb* \rb Keziah|קְצִיעָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb and his third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֖ית\rb*\rb |קֶ֥רֶן\rb* \rb Keren-happuch|הַפּֽוּךְ׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb No|וְלֹ֨א\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb as beautiful|יָפ֛וֹת\rb* \rb as Job’s|אִיּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb daughters|כִּבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb could be found|נִמְצָ֜א\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and their father|אֲבִיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb granted|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֧ם\rb* \rb an inheritance|נַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb After|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֔את\rb*, \rb Job|אִיּוֹב֙\rb* \rb lived|וַיְחִ֤י\rb* \rb 140|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּרְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his children|בָּנָיו֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and their|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb children|בָנָ֔יו\rb* \rb to the fourth|אַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb generation|דֹּרֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb And so Job|אִיּ֔וֹב\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb*, \rb old|זָקֵ֖ן\rb* \rb and full|וּשְׂבַ֥ע\rb* \rb of years|יָמִֽים׃\rb*.
